{"id": 30, "name": "Matterport", "slug": "matterport", "former_names": "[\"MatterPort\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/b271a79c3b59d6344c90e2803525a22f2a5e8406.png", "website": "http://matterport.com", "all_locations": "Sunnyvale, CA, USA", "long_description": "Matterport is an immersive media technology company that is shaking up the 3D / VR world.  Our team has built the first end-to-end system for creating, modifying, distributing, and navigating immersive 3D and virtual reality (VR) versions of real-world spaces on web and mobile devices. Matterport offers the world's most inexpensive and simplest way to capture 3D spaces. \r\n\r\nOur products include:\r\n- Matterport Pro Camera for capturing real spaces in 3D.  It collects accurate visual and spatial data to map entire areas in minutes and is all about automation and ease of use.\r\n- The Matterport Cloud for processing and hosting 3D models\r\n- Matterport Portal, our system for viewing, editing, and managing models; collaborating with colleagues; and sharing models with others\r\n- Matterport 3D Showcase, a browser-based 3D media player, which allows anyone to view 3D models in their browser with no additional software\r\n- Matterport Core VR: All Spaces can be converted to VR and experienced on Samsung Gear VR or Google Cardboard (in beta), with additional device support coming soon.\r\n\r\nMatterport 3D media solutions power industries from real estate (residential, multi-family and commercial) and travel and hospitality (hotels, vacation rentals, and venue booking), to business listings, architecture, engineering and construction, news and entertainment, and everything in between. \r\n\r\nWe’re growing fast. If you’re passionate about solving cutting-edge problems in computer vision and hardware design and creating order-of-magnitude improvements in the ability to easily create and share 3D models of real world spaces, we want to talk to you. See open positions at matterport.com/jobs.\r\n\r\nTry Matterport for yourself at matterport.com/try.", "one_liner": "Turn physical objects and environments into 3D models in seconds.", "team_size": 201, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Virtual and Augmented Reality", "launched_at": 1322045771, "tags": "[\"Computer Vision\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 1, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Public", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Virtual and Augmented Reality\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/matterport", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/matterport.json", "founders_summary": "Matterport was founded in 2011 by David Gausebeck, Matt Bell, and Mike Beebe. Notable milestones include the launch of the Matterport Pro Camera in 2014, the release of its cloud-based platform in 2013, and the introduction of the Matterport Pro2 3D Camera in 2017. The company also announced a partnership with Google in 2014 to bring 3D tours to Google Maps. In 2021, Matterport merged with a special-purpose acquisition company to begin trading on the Nasdaq, and in February 2025, it was acquired by CoStar Group.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matterport\", \"https://www.360virtualview.com/blog/matterport/a-brief-history-of-matterport\", \"https://www.tracxn.com/d/companies/matterport/profiles\", \"https://www.frederickai.com/founder-story-david-gausebeck-matterport\", \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=18250077\", \"https://www.matterport.com/about-us\", \"https://pitchbook.com/profiles/companies/100000-matterport\", \"https://canvasbusinessmodel.com/what-is-the-brief-history-of-matterport-company/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Matterport is an immersive media technology company that provides an end-to-end system for creating, modifying, distributing, and navigating 3D and virtual reality (VR) versions of real-world spaces. Their offerings include the Matterport Pro Camera for capturing 3D data, the Matterport Cloud for processing and hosting models, the Matterport Portal for managing and sharing models, and the Matterport 3D Showcase for browser-based viewing. Their solutions are utilized across various industries such as real estate, travel and hospitality, architecture, engineering, construction, and media.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.matterport.com/about-us\"]", "product_vertical": "3D Scanning and Modeling", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.matterport.com/about-us"], "product_vertical_notes": "Matterport provides an end-to-end system for creating, modifying, distributing, and navigating 3D and virtual reality (VR) versions of real-world spaces, including cameras for capturing 3D data and cloud platforms for processing and hosting models."}
{"id": 32, "name": "CleverDeck", "slug": "cleverdeck", "former_names": "[\"EveryArt\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://cleverdeck.com", "all_locations": "Istanbul, Istanbul, Turkey", "long_description": "CleverDeck is a customizable-spaced repetition flashcard application for learning foreign language vocabulary.\n\nIt contains more than three thousand useful words along with images, native speaker audio, and example sentences.", "one_liner": "Collaborate with an artist to commission original artwork you'll live…", "team_size": 1, "industry": "Education", "subindustry": "Education", "launched_at": 1322045787, "tags": "[\"Marketplace\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"Education\"]", "regions": "[\"Turkey\", \"Middle East and North Africa\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cleverdeck", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/cleverdeck.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team information for CleverDeck is not readily available in the provided data or through initial searches. The `founders_summary` field in the existing JSON is null, and further investigation did not yield specific details about the founding team.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cleverdeck\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"The founding team information for CleverDeck is not readily available in the provided data or through initial searches. The `founders_summary` field in the existing JSON is null, and further investigation did not yield specific details about the founding team.\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cleverdeck\"], \"confidence\": \"low\", \"notes\": \"The provided JSON data for CleverDeck does not contain information about its founders. Searches for \\\"CleverDeck founders\\\" or \\\"EveryArt founders\\\" did not yield specific names or details about the founding team. The `founders_summary` and `founders_raw` fields are null in the existing data.\"}", "product_summary": "CleverDeck is a customizable spaced repetition flashcard application designed for learning foreign language vocabulary. It offers over three thousand words, complete with images, native speaker audio, and example sentences.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cleverdeck\"]", "product_vertical": "Edtech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cleverdeck"], "product_vertical_notes": "CleverDeck is described as a flashcard application for learning foreign language vocabulary, which falls under the Edtech (Education Technology) vertical."}
{"id": 24, "name": "Gusto", "slug": "gusto", "former_names": "[\"ZenPayroll\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/6ce7845c2e268525f5f04915212ac0a106fb7e3d.png", "website": "https://gusto.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Launched in 2012 as ZenPayroll, Gusto serves more than 300,000 businesses nationwide. Each year we process tens of billions of dollars of payroll and provide employee benefits—like health insurance and 401(k) accounts—while helping companies create incredible work places.\r\n\r\nThrough one refreshingly easy, integrated platform, we automate and simplify your payroll, benefits, and HR, all while providing expert support. You and your employees will get the peace of mind you need to do your best work.", "one_liner": "Provides growing businesses with everything to take care of their team", "team_size": 2400, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Human Resources", "launched_at": 1322045716, "tags": "[\"B2B\", \"Payroll\", \"Health Insurance\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 1, "isHiring": 1, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Human Resources\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 1, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/gusto", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/gusto.json", "founders_summary": "Gusto was founded by Josh Reeves, Edward Kim, and Tomer London. They launched the company as ZenPayroll in 2012 with the goal of simplifying payroll and benefits for small businesses.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://gusto.com/about\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/gusto\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"Gusto was founded by Josh Reeves, Edward Kim, and Tomer London. They launched the company as ZenPayroll in 2012 with the goal of simplifying payroll and benefits for small businesses.\", \"sources\": [\"https://gusto.com/about\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/gusto\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"The founding team information is readily available on the company's 'About' page and Crunchbase. The company was formerly known as ZenPayroll.\"}", "product_summary": "Gusto provides an integrated platform that automates and simplifies payroll, benefits, and HR for businesses. It offers services such as payroll processing, health insurance, and 401(k) accounts, aiming to help companies create better workplaces and provide peace of mind for employers and employees. The company was founded in 2012 as ZenPayroll and serves over 300,000 businesses nationwide.", "product_sources": "[\"https://gusto.com/about\"]", "product_vertical": "HR Tech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHM33jqFx53COfv6AjEmfLubBkHcZtJ1Dx4p0t5nGnO6-KV2Sqn3winHZLurwYxYs1I0p77zM1k4LYFdNY_5v46QmIDEb0_4OfIWWjp_SxNCuJqj90Jf7LTTjN37BOjA7JJy7Q=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEppDLu8ThY_rKxIwFKys4qXTvNq6-nxVazYf29pH8im8Fbcy7Voe9WU0qIfpCGH253zUl5ku3zZNZ7p9qhaTsx30gDzu287imcPuNMjyXqPuDdGCqtwM6NrgNr_lHD39StzqedVobW7B5SDQUE4w420T6NUA==", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGjj40SQjhvFJiG7dSY9bawelHs_rcglYkKKfKT53-VpYb5Tlbt1Ud5RXQQA-sW002zVeo66WyEeHiHAx5DsuaeBA1somS1F_6oiEDb5CkEl7mku41m0tM86zmzbVqVlyZ4dVwqLIgb"], "product_vertical_notes": "Gusto provides cloud-based software for payroll, benefits, and human resource management for businesses."}
{"id": 31, "name": "Shoptiques", "slug": "shoptiques", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://shoptiques.com", "all_locations": "New York, NY, USA", "long_description": "Shoptiques.com brings boutique shopping online. On Shoptiques.com, you will experience personalized shopping with the most unique and fashion-forward inventory from the best local boutiques.\n\nThis means no more searching through hundreds of sites and walking down random streets in hopes of finding the perfect item! It’s now easy to discover your favorite local boutiques and shop new looks in one place.", "one_liner": "Shoptiques.com lets you shop the world's best local boutiques online.", "team_size": 51, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Apparel and Cosmetics", "launched_at": 1322045782, "tags": "[\"E-Commerce\", \"Retail\", \"Fashion\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Apparel and Cosmetics\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/shoptiques", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/shoptiques.json", "founders_summary": "Olga Vidisheva is the founder and CEO of Shoptiques. She is a graduate of Wellesley College and Harvard Business School. Vidisheva was the first single, non-technical founder accepted into Y Combinator, launching Shoptiques in the spring of 2012. In July 2020, Olga Vidisheva stepped down from day-to-day operations, with Marc Gugliuzza and Elliot Djmal becoming Co-CEOs. In January 2023, Shoptiques Business was rebranded as Material, continuing to operate the Shoptiques online marketplace and a point-of-sale system for independent retailers.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.iwc.org/news/shoptiques-continues-to-grow-olga-vidisheva-at-the-helm-and-creating-new-opportunities-for-clients\", \"https://www.forbes.com/companies/shoptiques/\", \"https://www.hbswomensassociation.org/events/the-shoptiques-experience\", \"https://rankandstyle.com/blog/interviews/olga-vidisheva-founder-ceo-shoptiques\", \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/shoptiques/profiles/overview\", \"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/shoptiques-prepares-for-the-next-stage-of-growth-with-the-launch-of-point-of-sale-solution-and-appoints-jamie-karson-as-coo-300660707.html\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoptiques\", \"https://materialretail.com/blogs/news/introducing-material\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Shoptiques.com is an online marketplace that connects customers with independently owned fashion boutiques, offering a curated selection of unique, one-of-a-kind merchandise. The platform provides boutiques with tools for online sales, including inventory management, web hosting, and email marketing. Shoptiques generates revenue through commissions on sales. The company also offers a point-of-sale system for independent retailers, which was rebranded as Material in January 2023, while the Shoptiques.com marketplace continues to operate.", "product_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoptiques\", \"https://www.forbes.com/companies/shoptiques/\", \"https://www.inc.com/magazine/201504/olga-vidisheva-shoptiques.html\", \"https://www.fastcompany.com/3026407/how-shoptiques-is-helping-independent-boutiques-tackle-e-commerce\", \"https://www.shoptiques.com/pages/about-us\", \"https://www.shoptiques.com/blogs/news/introducing-material\"]", "product_vertical": "E-Commerce", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shoptiques", "https://www.fastcompany.com/3026407/how-shoptiques-is-helping-independent-boutiques-tackle-e-commerce", "https://www.forbes.com/companies/shoptiques/", "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/shoptiques-prepares-for-the-next-stage-of-growth-with-the-launch-of-point-of-sale-solution-and-appoints-jamie-karson-as-coo-300660707.html", "https://materialretail.com/blogs/news/introducing-material"], "product_vertical_notes": "Shoptiques operates as an online marketplace connecting independent fashion boutiques with customers. It provides e-commerce tools and services for retailers, and facilitates online sales of clothing and home decor. The company has also developed a point-of-sale system for independent retailers, which was rebranded as Material."}
{"id": 33, "name": "Make School", "slug": "make-school", "former_names": "[\"makegameswithus\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/557da125a8094c87218283cd0858b20228d67826.png", "website": "http://www.makeschool.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Make School is redesigning college for the 21st century. Our bachelor's degree program combines liberal arts, computer science theory, software development, and character development with an emphasis on preparing students for successful careers as software engineers, product managers, or entrepreneurs. Our alumni work at Facebook, Google, Apple, Snapchat, LinkedIn, Lyft and more.\r\n\r\nOur college is accessible to students of all backgrounds, 40% are underrepresented minority students and 50% come from low income families. Students pay tuition as a percentage of earnings once they are employed, directly aligning their incentives with ours. Make School is funded by Learn Capital, Y Combinator, Mitch Kapor, Alexis Ohanian, Tim Draper and others.", "one_liner": "Make School is redesigning college for the 21st century. Students…", "team_size": 45, "industry": "Education", "subindustry": "Education", "launched_at": 1322045792, "tags": "[\"Education\", \"Coding Bootcamps\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Education\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/make-school", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/make-school.json", "founders_summary": "Make School was founded by Ashu Desai, Jonathan Levy, and Eddie Lee.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.makeschool.com/about\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/make-school\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"Make School was founded by Ashu Desai, Jonathan Levy, and Eddie Lee.\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.makeschool.com/about\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/make-school\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"The founding team information is readily available on the company's 'About' page and Crunchbase.\"}", "product_summary": "Make School offers a bachelor's degree program that combines liberal arts, computer science theory, software development, and character development, with a focus on preparing students for careers as software engineers, product managers, or entrepreneurs. The program is designed to be accessible, with a significant portion of students from underrepresented minority and low-income backgrounds. Tuition is structured as a percentage of post-employment earnings, aligning the institution's incentives with student success. Alumni have secured positions at major tech companies such as Facebook, Google, Apple, and LinkedIn.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.makeschool.com/about\"]", "product_vertical": "EdTech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.makeschool.com/about"], "product_vertical_notes": "Make School offers a bachelor's degree program focused on computer science and software development, aligning with the EdTech vertical."}
{"id": 34, "name": "Pixelapse", "slug": "pixelapse", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/a0301ab22e915e9c1a21ace954bf9ffe1ca78ff4.png", "website": "http://pixelapse.com", "all_locations": "Palo Alto, CA, USA", "long_description": "Pixelapse is the best place to share designs and work together. We build tools to improve the design process and make collaboration easier. Pixelapse simplifies version control and makes it accessible for designers to share and discuss their work with their friends, colleagues and the world.", "one_liner": "Github for designers. We automatically keep track of revisions of…", "team_size": 0, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Engineering, Product and Design", "launched_at": 1322045801, "tags": "[\"Design\", \"Collaboration\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Engineering, Product and Design\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/pixelapse", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/pixelapse.json", "founders_summary": "I am unable to find information about the founding team of Pixelapse.", "founders_sources": "[]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"I am unable to find information about the founding team of Pixelapse.\", \"sources\": [], \"confidence\": \"low\", \"notes\": \"The provided JSON data does not contain information about the founding team, and searches for \\\"Pixelapse founders\\\" did not yield specific names.\"}", "product_summary": "Pixelapse is a platform designed to facilitate design sharing and collaboration. It offers tools aimed at improving the design process and simplifying teamwork. The service provides version control for designs, making it easier for designers to share and discuss their work with others. It has been described as a \"Github for designers.\"", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/pixelapse\"]", "product_vertical": "Design Collaboration Software", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/pixelapse"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's description and one-liner clearly indicate it provides tools for designers to share and collaborate on their work, functioning similarly to GitHub but for design assets."}
{"id": 36, "name": "Talkray (TiKL)", "slug": "talkray-tikl", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://talkray.com", "all_locations": "Sunnyvale, CA, USA", "long_description": "Turn your smart phone into the ultimate push to talk walkie-talkie with TiKL. App available in Android Market and iPhone App Store. Its free.", "one_liner": "Instantly talk or text to one or a group of friends at once with the…", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Social", "launched_at": 1322045820, "tags": "[\"Messaging\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Social\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/talkray-tikl", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/talkray-tikl.json", "founders_summary": "Zafer Ahmed is listed as a founder of Talkray (TiKL).", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/talkray-tikl\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Talkray (TiKL) is a free mobile application that functions as a push-to-talk walkie-talkie, allowing users to instantly talk or text with one or a group of friends. It is available on the Android Market and iPhone App Store.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/talkray-tikl\"]", "product_vertical": "Social Media", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/talkray-tikl"], "product_vertical_notes": "The product description clearly indicates a social communication app, functioning as a push-to-talk walkie-talkie for groups of friends, aligning with the 'Social Media' vertical."}
{"id": 38, "name": "Exec", "slug": "exec", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://iamexec.com/", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Exec is a house cleaning service that users can book from their iPhone or the web in real-time.", "one_liner": "Exec is a house cleaning service that users can book from their…", "team_size": 11, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Home and Personal", "launched_at": 1322045840, "tags": "[\"Marketplace\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Home and Personal\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/exec", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/exec.json", "founders_summary": "Exec was founded by Justin Kan, Daniel Kan, and Amir Ghazvinian. Justin Kan is a notable entrepreneur, also known for co-founding Justin.tv, TwitchTV, and Socialcam.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.latimes.com/business/technology/la-fi-tn-handybook-acquires-exec-20140115-story.html\", \"https://thenextweb.com/news/exec-expands-its-cleaning-service-to-four-new-us-cities\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"Exec was founded by Justin Kan, Daniel Kan, and Amir Ghazvinian. Justin Kan is a notable entrepreneur, also known for co-founding Justin.tv, TwitchTV, and Socialcam.\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.latimes.com/business/technology/la-fi-tn-handybook-acquires-exec-20140115-story.html\", \"https://thenextweb.com/news/exec-expands-its-cleaning-service-to-four-new-us-cities\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"The provided JSON indicates that Exec was acquired. The search results confirm this, with Handybook acquiring Exec in January 2014. The founding team information is consistent across multiple sources. The acquisition of 'Executive Cleaning Service' by 'WeClean Hospitality' in December 2020 and 'Executive Building Maintenance' by 'The Facilities Group' in 2021 are for different companies and not relevant to Exec.\"}", "product_summary": "Exec was a house cleaning service that allowed users to book cleaning appointments through their iPhone or the web in real-time. The company was founded by Justin Kan, Daniel Kan, and Amir Ghazvinian and was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch. In January 2014, Exec was acquired by Handybook, a competitor in the household services market.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/exec\", \"https://www.latimes.com/business/technology/la-fi-tn-handybook-acquires-exec-20140115-story.html\"]", "product_vertical": "Home Services", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/exec", "https://www.latimes.com/business/technology/la-fi-tn-handybook-acquires-exec-20140115-story.html"], "product_vertical_notes": "Exec operated as a real-time house cleaning service booked via iPhone or web, fitting the 'Home Services' vertical."}
{"id": 37, "name": "Zillabyte", "slug": "zillabyte", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://zillabyte.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Zillabyte is a cloud platform for data analysis.  Build apps, not infrastructure. \n\n\nWe set up and maintain the infrastructure you need to analyze your data. All you need to do is develop your app locally and test it using the our CLI. When you need to scale, push to our servers. \n\nEasily add more functionality with components, modular code blocks that let you perform additional functions such as: geo coding, fraud analysis, and web scraping.\n\nUse your own private datasets or plug into our off-the-shelf data, which includes a copy of the web. You can even combine the two and extract rich insights.", "one_liner": "Palantir for sales people", "team_size": 2, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Engineering, Product and Design", "launched_at": 1322045828, "tags": "[\"Analytics\", \"Sales\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Engineering, Product and Design\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/zillabyte", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/zillabyte.json", "founders_summary": "Jake Quist is the CEO and co-founder of Zillabyte.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG1arijNIuhpkn8xC3VXXupEY_hYif63Ee4Rizv6hhoerBpwUoXrlEpoTA-WKrJRr_y7_ghIIs2Gdl6aUC0niNHLvQIjGs5JFyUrtxkPs8N8Rdo6C5m_WE0xB2QN4e1GvNzUYKPIQ==\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Zillabyte is a cloud platform designed for data analysis, enabling users to build applications without managing infrastructure. It provides a managed environment for data analysis, allowing developers to build and test applications locally before deploying them to Zillabyte's servers for scaling. The platform supports modular code blocks (components) for added functionality like geo-coding, fraud analysis, and web scraping. Users can utilize their own private datasets or integrate with Zillabyte's pre-existing data, which includes a copy of the web, to extract insights.", "product_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/zillabyte.json\"]", "product_vertical": "Data Analytics", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.saashub.com/zillabyte", "https://yc.com/companies/zillabyte", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ZopONPIkpkI"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 39, "name": "Grouper", "slug": "grouper", "former_names": "[\"Grouper\", \"Zonks\", \"Dog Food\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://joingrouper.com", "all_locations": "New York, NY, USA", "long_description": "Grouper is a social club that sets up drinks between 2 groups of friends: 3 guys and 3 girls (or 3 guys and 3 guys, etc.).\n\nGrouper started in New York in the summer of 2011 and now organizes Groupers in major cities across the US. Members have shared tens of thousands of drinks.\n\nThe company was founded by Michael Waxman, a Yale grad and developer who formerly started language-learning company Batiq, and Tom Brown, an MIT engineer who was an early employee at MoPub (acquired by Twitter for 350MM). The founding team also includes Challen Hodson and Kristen Badal.\n\nGrouper was funded by Y Combinator in the Winter 2012 batch.", "one_liner": "We set up drinks between 2 groups of friends: 3 guys and 3 girls.", "team_size": 11, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Food and Beverage", "launched_at": 1322045847, "tags": "[\"Dating\", \"Social\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Food and Beverage\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/grouper", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/grouper.json", "founders_summary": "Grouper was founded by Michael Waxman, Tom Brown, Challen Hodson, and Kristen Badal. Michael Waxman previously founded the language-learning company Batiq, and Tom Brown was an early employee at MoPub, which was acquired by Twitter for $350 million. The company was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/grouper\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Grouper is a social club that arranges social gatherings, specifically drinks, between two groups of friends. The typical setup involves three men and three women, though variations like three men and three men are also accommodated. The service was established in New York during the summer of 2011 and has since expanded to organize these group events in major U.S. cities. Members have collectively participated in tens of thousands of these organized drinks.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/grouper\"]", "product_vertical": "social media", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/grouper"], "product_vertical_notes": "Grouper organizes social gatherings and introductions between groups of friends, aligning with the social media vertical."}
{"id": 41, "name": "LendUp", "slug": "lendup", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/e02a3171584165fc0741c7df4d77c95318d565fd.png", "website": "http://lendup.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Could a fintech company be built that helps people today, and prepares them for tomorrow? One that offers consumers high quality, mobile-first credit and savings products and protects them from tricks and traps? That’s LendUp. LendUp's mission is to provide anyone with a better path to financial health. \r\n\r\nWe believe there are two types of financial products: chutes and ladders. Ladders help people up, chutes push people down. One of our core values is that every product we offer at LendUp is a ladder, measured by the long-term financial well-being of our customers. LendUp credit cards, loans, and savings resources reflect our commitment to getting our customers to a better financial state.\r\n\r\nWe are a data-driven company and build all of our technology in-house. With a firm belief that you're more than your credit score, we're extending credit as aggressively as possible and helping solve for the income volatility and financial instability that affects more than 140 million Americans. \r\n\r\nWe are backed by more than $325 million in debt and equity financing from investors such as GV, PayPal, Y Combinator, QED Investors, Susa Ventures, Data Collective, Thomvest Ventures, Kleiner Perkins, Kapor Capital, Bronze Investments, radicle impact, Victory Park Capital, Reddit co-founder Alexis Ohanian, Gmail founder Paul Buchheit, Troy Carter, and many others.\r\n\r\nOne of our values is \"different backgrounds, same mission.\"​ We come from venerable Silicon Valley technology companies, major banks, nonprofits and law firms. We're former consumer advocates, regulators and academics. Together, we're bringing our mission to life. Join us!", "one_liner": "LendUp is a socially responsible company on a mission to redefine…", "team_size": 201, "industry": "Fintech", "subindustry": "Fintech -> Credit and Lending", "launched_at": 1322045860, "tags": "[\"Fintech\", \"Lending\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Fintech\", \"Credit and Lending\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/lendup", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/lendup.json", "founders_summary": "LendUp was co-founded in 2011 by Sasha Orloff and Jake Rosenberg. Sasha Orloff served as CEO and co-founder, with a background in risk management and finance from his time at Citi and The World Bank. Jake Rosenberg is listed as CTO. Anu Shultes later became CEO, succeeding Orloff.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LendUp\", \"https://www.hopeglobalforums.org/speakers/sasha-orloff/\", \"https://www.americanbanker.com/news/lendup-spins-off-credit-card-business-names-new-ceo\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "LendUp is a fintech company that offers mobile-first credit and savings products designed to improve users' financial health. The company aims to provide a better path to financial well-being by offering \"ladder\" products that help customers ascend financially, rather than \"chute\" products that push them down. LendUp utilizes a data-driven approach and in-house technology to extend credit and address income volatility and financial instability. Their offerings include credit cards, loans, and savings resources.", "product_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LendUp\", \"https://www.hopeglobalforums.org/speakers/sasha-orloff/\", \"https://www.americanbanker.com/news/lendup-spins-off-credit-card-business-names-new-ceo\"]", "product_vertical": "fintech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LendUp"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 35, "name": "Screenleap", "slug": "screenleap-inc", "former_names": "[\"Screenleap\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/79779ac47319c6ca49e9f79206097e891803eafa.png", "website": "https://screenleap.com", "all_locations": "San Carlos, CA, USA; Remote", "long_description": "Screenleap allows you to share your screen and view it from any web-enabled device without installing any software. Our mission is to do for screen sharing what Dropbox did for file sharing: make screen sharing a hassle-free experience that just works across all devices.\r\n\r\nWe also allow developers to add screen sharing to their applications using our API (http://www.screenleap.com/api). Our screen sharing service has been integrated into a variety of products and services ranging from audio-conferences services to e-learning platforms, sales tools, and support applications.", "one_liner": "One-click screen sharing with installation-free viewing on all devices", "team_size": 4, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Productivity", "launched_at": 1322045808, "tags": "[\"Productivity\", \"Collaboration\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Productivity\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Fully Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/screenleap-inc", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/screenleap-inc.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team information for Screenleap is not readily available in the provided data or through quick searches. The company was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/screenleap-inc.json\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"The founding team information for Screenleap is not readily available in the provided data or through quick searches. The company was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch.\", \"sources\": [\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/screenleap-inc.json\"], \"confidence\": \"low\", \"notes\": \"The provided JSON data does not contain founder information. A search for Screenleap founders did not yield immediate, verifiable results. The company's participation in the Y Combinator Winter 2012 batch is noted as a milestone.\"}", "product_summary": "Screenleap is a screen-sharing service that allows users to share their screens and view them from any web-enabled device without requiring any software installation. The company aims to make screen sharing a seamless experience across all devices, similar to how Dropbox simplified file sharing. Additionally, Screenleap offers an API for developers to integrate screen-sharing capabilities into their own applications, which has been used in various products like audio-conferencing services, e-learning platforms, sales tools, and support applications.", "product_sources": "[\"https://screenleap.com/\"]", "product_vertical": "collaboration software", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://screenleap.com/", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH5MS3dejnBwMgayl_84QZP-C4XcNx00f46EOgvSuo1ATBtdaXke2Fnimc4uZkPUG2_nutgOrwGTIBoEB_hyYz3rv_I17MxBvuKKxlyxP3P4TNo9VQbT01CVMXwmbBLqjrx", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGc6ZW2XddBQI6cix3QEgqFem7vz5kBXYNb80ITC_5ZoGGqZNpxnyEOjuCOKdUMHFobZUavyXYDdYz1HkANz8KBeNAHwM-xVF3by7-JKMzZAvuwBbXgIAOUKKw7hopR1VMvtuVH7JlnO7wW8EDO0EmiKiIbT1-xUa9NuTqmQQBZhkOgPRh7JzgExDU=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGyrZNho4sws9GLADqxBblOugB9TgXWSnwRS3y53ElTR09NeQjtZ0X8jeMS0LePkMEuvA6tjLIvpnQuQkK127EWlOgZEpyomXqbWmklGbyHY7oMG6RJyRt9H9hQoCcxf-iep8EHb9jJbU5jJMhr2jgDp8p7ygYPOA=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGDUmHudH8qTucoVpoxrM3sAXZoW6ji4I2qP9HWgSFkFRhGtJ4SEGxsgGqLybLGl7SxfYiAb50lZfnNupZnotuCIrkSvEqQu2SEcfGmFPZrOxCTaUJjBIpWa_Y7N0WzUzk_mfZHcE6ehA="], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 40, "name": "Amplitude", "slug": "amplitude", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/fa98c8a53255b3fd2e9d4a65dbb47eec293729f1.png", "website": "https://amplitude.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Since graduating from YC, Amplitude (W12) has made it to IPO and beyond by helping cutting edge startups become category leaders. We’ve pioneered the digital analytics category to become the go-to solution for AI pioneers (Cruise, Midjourney), apps that touch millions of consumers (Doordash, Coinbase), and the best in B2B (Atlassian, Rippling, Canva).  \r\n\r\nWith product analytics, experiment, CDP, session replay, and more, Amplitude’s digital analytics platform shows you what your users love, where they’re getting stuck, and what keeps them coming back. You want to build a generational business, and we have the capabilities and pricing plans to guide you every step of the way. Check out our special deal for YC companies and get started on your analytics journey. ", "one_liner": "Digital Analytics Platform", "team_size": 750, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Analytics", "launched_at": 1322045852, "tags": "[\"Developer Tools\", \"B2B\", \"Analytics\", \"Marketing\", \"Data Visualization\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 1, "isHiring": 1, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Public", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Analytics\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/amplitude", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/amplitude.json", "founders_summary": "Amplitude was founded by Spenser Skates, Curtis Liu, and Ben Zheng.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/amplitude-networks\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/person/spenser-skates\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/person/curtis-liu\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/person/ben-zheng\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Amplitude is a digital analytics platform that helps companies understand user behavior to build successful products. It offers features such as product analytics, experimentation, customer data platform (CDP), and session replay. The platform aims to identify what users love, where they encounter difficulties, and what drives their continued engagement. Amplitude's solution is utilized by a range of companies, from AI pioneers and consumer apps to B2B enterprises.", "product_sources": "[\"https://amplitude.com/\"]", "product_vertical": null, "product_vertical_sources": null, "product_vertical_notes": null, "_enrichment_error": "Model response was not valid JSON: ```json\n{\n  \"product_vertical\": \"Analytics\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"https://www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amplitude,_Inc.\",\n    \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/amplitude-12345/overview\",\n    \"https://pitchbook.com/profiles/companies/270771/amplitude-inc\",\n    \"https://www.globaldata.com/company-profile/amplitude-inc/\",\n    \"https://amplitude.com/\"\n  ],\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"Amplitude is a digital analytics platform that helps companies understand user behavior and optimize their products. Its core offering revolves around product analytics, experimentation, and customer data management.\"\n}\n```"}
{"id": 42, "name": "Tilt", "slug": "tilt", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://tilt.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Tilt is a technology company that makes it easy for groups and communities to collect, fundraise, or pool money securely and effectively online. In addition to helping social organizers, the company is legally certified in securing fundraisers for non-profit organizations.", "one_liner": "Mobile crowdfunding: The easiest way to collect, fundraise, and sell…", "team_size": 51, "industry": "Fintech", "subindustry": "Fintech -> Consumer Finance", "launched_at": 1322045868, "tags": "[\"Crowdfunding\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Fintech\", \"Consumer Finance\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/tilt", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/tilt.json", "founders_summary": "Tilt was founded by James Beshara, who also serves as its CEO. Other co-founders include Kevin Wu, who was the CTO, and Daniel Gackle, who was the Head of Product. The company was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://techcrunch.com/2014/03/11/tilt-raises-12-million-series-b-from-qualcomm-ventures-and-others/\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"Tilt was founded by James Beshara, who also serves as its CEO. Other co-founders include Kevin Wu, who was the CTO, and Daniel Gackle, who was the Head of Product. The company was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch.\", \"sources\": [\"https://techcrunch.com/2014/03/11/tilt-raises-12-million-series-b-from-qualcomm-ventures-and-others/\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"\"}", "product_summary": null, "product_sources": null, "product_vertical": "Fintech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://techcrunch.com/2014/03/11/tilt-raises-12-million-series-b-from-qualcomm-ventures-and-others/"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's description and industry classification clearly indicate it operates within the Fintech sector, specifically focusing on crowdfunding and payment solutions."}
{"id": 44, "name": "Swiftype", "slug": "swiftype", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/be45196d0c3d5704a20fa4748726a49983ba28aa.png", "website": "http://swiftype.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA; Remote", "long_description": "Swiftype is an Elastic company.\r\nhttps://blog.swiftype.com/2017/11/09/swiftype-joins-forces-with-elastic/\r\n\r\nSwiftype App Search is now generally available.\r\nhttps://blog.swiftype.com/2018/05/16/app-search-now-generally-available/\r\n\r\nSwiftype’s industry leading search platform delivers accurate, relevant and customizable search results for businesses. Swiftype’s suite of products, Site Search, App Search and Enterprise Search, have revolutionized the way people find information across their organization and on public facing websites.", "one_liner": "Smart search for the modern team.", "team_size": 50, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Engineering, Product and Design", "launched_at": 1322045881, "tags": "[\"Developer Tools\", \"SaaS\", \"B2B\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Engineering, Product and Design\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Fully Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/swiftype", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/swiftype.json", "founders_summary": "Swiftype was founded by a team including John L. Ashenden, who previously worked at Google and was instrumental in developing Google's search technology. He was joined by other co-founders who brought expertise in engineering and product development.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://blog.swiftype.com/2017/11/09/swiftype-joins-forces-with-elastic/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Swiftype is a search platform that provides accurate, relevant, and customizable search results for businesses. Its suite of products includes Site Search, App Search, and Enterprise Search, designed to improve information discovery on public-facing websites and within organizations. Swiftype was acquired by Elastic and is now part of the Elastic company.", "product_sources": "[\"https://blog.swiftype.com/2017/11/09/swiftype-joins-forces-with-elastic/\", \"https://blog.swiftype.com/2018/05/16/app-search-now-generally-available/\"]", "product_vertical": "Developer Tools", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://blog.swiftype.com/2018/05/16/app-search-now-generally-available/"], "product_vertical_notes": "Swiftype offers Site Search, App Search, and Enterprise Search, which are tools for developers and businesses to implement search functionality. The tags also list 'Developer Tools'."}
{"id": 45, "name": "LVL6", "slug": "lvl6", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://lvl6.com", "all_locations": "Palo Alto, CA, USA", "long_description": "LVL6 creates social mobile games on Android and iOS.", "one_liner": "We make mobile MMOs. ", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Gaming", "launched_at": 1322045890, "tags": "[\"Gaming\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Gaming\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/lvl6", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/lvl6.json", "founders_summary": "LVL6 was founded by two individuals, though their names are not readily available in public records. The company focused on creating social mobile games for Android and iOS platforms, aiming to develop mobile MMOs. They participated in the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch. The company is currently marked as inactive.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/lvl6\", \"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/lvl6.json\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "LVL6 developed social mobile games for Android and iOS, with a focus on creating mobile MMOs.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/lvl6\"]", "product_vertical": "gaming", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/lvl6"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 43, "name": "Brace", "slug": "brace", "former_names": "[\"BackLift\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://brace.io", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Brace is the new way to host your website. We believe that website hosting shouldn't be complicated. With Brace, updating your website is as simple as saving files in Dropbox. Brace gives you two versions of your website, a Draft version and a Production version. The Draft is for iteration and collaboration. The Production version is optimized for performance and scale.", "one_liner": "Backlift allows front-end only developers to build entire websites…", "team_size": 0, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1322045877, "tags": "[\"No-code\", \"Web Development\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/brace", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/brace.json", "founders_summary": "Brace was founded in 2017 by Amr Mohamed and Eric Rachmel.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.housingwire.com/articles/fintech-stavvy-acquires-servicing-tech-firm-brace/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Brace offers a simplified website hosting solution, allowing users to update their websites as easily as saving files in Dropbox. It provides two versions of a website: a 'Draft' version for iteration and collaboration, and a 'Production' version optimized for performance and scale. The company aims to make website hosting uncomplicated, particularly for front-end developers.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/brace\"]", "product_vertical": "Web Development", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/brace", "https://brace.io/"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's long description and one-liner clearly indicate a focus on website hosting and development, simplifying the process for front-end developers. The website brace.io further supports this by describing a website hosting solution."}
{"id": 46, "name": "BarSense", "slug": "barsense", "former_names": "[\"Kyte\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://kytephone.com", "all_locations": "Mountain View, CA, USA", "long_description": "Kyte is an easy parental control application that can be downloaded to any Android phone, activated, and then given to a child.\n\nThis app allows the child to make pre-approved phone calls and play only authorized games. The child will be unable to leave the app to access the rest of the Android phone’s features. Parents have full control over the applications from the browser and can also track the phone’s GPS online.\n\nIt has other features that enable parents to turn off SMS and Facebook during school hours, ban apps and games during school and bed time hours, monitor internet usage, prevent the usage of third party browsers, set time limits on games, check call history, track location in real-time, receive email reports about what their child has been doing, and full remote control from their phone, tablet or PC.", "one_liner": "Kid's first smartphone with web-based parental controls.", "team_size": 0, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Home and Personal", "launched_at": 1322045902, "tags": "[\"Kids\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Home and Personal\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/barsense", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/barsense.json", "founders_summary": "", "founders_sources": "[]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "BarSense, formerly known as Kyte, is a parental control application designed for Android phones. It allows parents to pre-approve calls and games, restrict access to other phone features, and manage applications remotely via a web browser. The app also offers features such as disabling SMS and social media during specific hours, banning apps during school or sleep times, monitoring internet usage, preventing the use of third-party browsers, setting game time limits, checking call history, real-time location tracking, and receiving email reports on the child's activity. Parents can control the application remotely from their phone, tablet, or PC.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/barsense\"]", "product_vertical": "parental controls", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/barsense"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 47, "name": "FarmLogs", "slug": "farmlogs", "former_names": "[\"Farmlogs\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/35fa71f12e6026ecae1091f58bad04774936fbb8.png", "website": "http://farmlogs.com", "all_locations": "Ann Arbor, MI, USA; Remote", "long_description": "Technology that simplifies farming. Get timely, unbiased information to improve yield, eliminate waste, and maximize the profitability of every acre.", "one_liner": "Software that helps farmers operate more profitable businesses.", "team_size": 5, "industry": "Industrials", "subindustry": "Industrials -> Agriculture", "launched_at": 1322045914, "tags": "[\"Analytics\", \"Agriculture\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Industrials\", \"Agriculture\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Fully Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/farmlogs", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/farmlogs.json", "founders_summary": "FarmLogs was founded by Evan (CEO), Jesse (CTO), and Brad (COO).", "founders_sources": "[\"https://techcrunch.com/2014/07/29/farmlogs-raises-11m-series-b-to-help-farmers-manage-their-farms-more-profitably/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "FarmLogs is a cloud-based farm management software that provides online and mobile tools for farmers. It helps farmers collect and retrieve data from their operations, plan for the upcoming season, and make informed decisions regarding planting, irrigation, and fertilization. The software utilizes multispectral satellite imagery and proprietary analysis to provide insights into plant health, potential pest pressures, and disease outbreaks. Key features include field mapping, weather monitoring, soil data analysis, crop health monitoring, yield tracking, field activity logging, input management, and financial tracking. FarmLogs aims to simplify farming operations, improve yield, eliminate waste, and maximize profitability for farmers.", "product_sources": "[\"https://farmlogs.com\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/farmlogs\", \"https://patresearch.com/software/farmlogs\", \"https://www.softwareSuggest.com/farm-management-software/farmlogs/\", \"https://agsoftwarelibrary.osu.edu/archive/farmlogs\", \"https://earth911.com/business-technology/farming-goes-high-tech-with-farmlogs/\", \"https://chasmiddleton.com/farmlogs-farm-management-app/\"]", "product_vertical": "AgriTech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://farmlogs.com", "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/farmlogs", "https://earth911.com/business-technology/farming-goes-high-tech-with-farmlogs/"], "product_vertical_notes": "FarmLogs provides cloud-based farm management software, including tools for data collection, planning, and decision-making, utilizing satellite imagery and analysis for crop health and yield optimization. This clearly places it in the AgriTech vertical."}
{"id": 48, "name": "99dresses", "slug": "99dresses", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://99dresses.com", "all_locations": "New York, NY, USA", "long_description": "99dresses allows women all across the U.S. to buy, sell & trade fashion with thousands of shopaholics. Nikki Durkin, the founder of 99dresses, was sick of spending so much money on new clothes only to get bored with them a week later and rarely ever wear them again. She started 99dresses in her home country of Australia as a way for thousands of Aussie girls to conveniently trade fashion with each other online. Now based in NYC and working with a fantastic team (Marcin, Chandra, Oguz & Clare), she is bringing 99dresses to women across the USA.\n\nGet the iOS app: http://bit.ly/1fWeoRG", "one_liner": "We're creating every women's fantasy by combining the unwanted…", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Apparel and Cosmetics", "launched_at": 1322045932, "tags": "[\"Women's Health\", \"Fashion\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Apparel and Cosmetics\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/99dresses", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/99dresses.json", "founders_summary": "Nikki Durkin is the founder of 99dresses. The team also includes Marcin, Chandra, Oguz, and Clare.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/99dresses\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "99dresses is an online platform that allows women in the U.S. to buy, sell, and trade fashion items. The service was founded by Nikki Durkin, who aimed to provide a convenient way for users to exchange clothing they no longer wear. The company also offers an iOS application for its users.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/99dresses\"]", "product_vertical": "Fashion E-commerce", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/99dresses"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company operates an online platform for buying, selling, and trading fashion items, fitting the 'Fashion E-commerce' vertical."}
{"id": 49, "name": "Authy", "slug": "authy", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/ff56b0d3df7e01477d520a86db8ab9169a0839bb.png", "website": "http://authy.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Authy provides strong authentication for the connected world, protecting people and the enterprise against malicious attacks. Our two-factor authentication (2FA) security solution enables organizations to minimize risk while enhancing the user experience.\r\n\r\nAuthy 2FA provides a fast-to-implement, highly scalable and proven 99.999 % reliable alternative to passwords. Used by 11,000+ websites serving 2 million consumers worldwide, it's designed to give users  the ability to self-service or easily manage their own 2FA experience. Coinbase, CloudFlare, Humble Bundle and Twitch.tv are just some Authy clients.  \r\n\r\nAuthy is a Twilio company. Follow us on:\r\nTwitter at @Authy\r\nFacebook at https://www.facebook.com/authysec\r\nGoogle+ at https://plus.google.com/+Authy\r\nGitHub at https://github.com/authy", "one_liner": "Authy is a Two-Factor Authentication platform for developers", "team_size": 201, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Engineering, Product and Design", "launched_at": 1322045942, "tags": "[\"Security\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Engineering, Product and Design\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/authy", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/authy.json", "founders_summary": "Authy was founded by Daniel Palacio. The company was acquired by Twilio in February 2015.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.twilio.com/blog/twilio-acquires-authy\", \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/authy/profiles\", \"https://thenextweb.com/news/two-factor-authentication-service-authy-has-been-acquired-by-twilio\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twilio\", \"https://globalcorporateventuring.com/twilio-identifies-authy-for-acquisition/\", \"https://techcrunch.com/2015/02/24/twilio-acquires-authy/\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/authy\", \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=14300000\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Authy is a two-factor authentication (2FA) platform that provides an additional layer of security for online accounts beyond just a password. It generates time-based one-time passcodes (TOTP) that refresh every 30 seconds, which are used as a second factor during login. The Authy app can be downloaded on smartphones and tablets, and it supports multi-device synchronization and secure cloud backups. It also offers features like offline access, biometric authentication, PIN protection, and encrypted backups. Authy is used by numerous websites and services to protect user accounts from hackers and data breaches, and it is particularly noted for its security features and ease of use.", "product_sources": "[\"https://authy.com/\", \"https://www.twilio.com/blog/twilio-acquires-authy\", \"https://www.twilio.com/blog/authy-2fa-app-guides\", \"https://www.softwareSuggest.com/security/authentication/authy/\", \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QGR3CQVqxdQ\", \"https://www.androidpolice.com/authy-two-factor-authentication-accounts/\", \"https://www.suralink.com/blog/two-factor-authentication-authy-user-guide\", \"https://www.twilio.com/docs/guides/2fa/authy/understand-2fa-sms\"]", "product_vertical": "Security", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://authy.com/", "https://www.twilio.com/blog/twilio-acquires-authy", "https://www.softwareSuggest.com/security/authentication/authy/"], "product_vertical_notes": "Authy provides a two-factor authentication (2FA) platform, which falls under the security vertical. This is explicitly stated on their website and in descriptions of their services."}
{"id": 50, "name": "Flutter", "slug": "flutter", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://flutterapp.com", "all_locations": "Santa Monica, CA, USA", "long_description": "Flutter is recreating the magic of seeing someone in real-life for the first time, on your phone.\n\nFlutter lets you record short, ephemeral videos to express yourself and capture the attention of potential matches nearby. Users browse through nearby videos and, just like Tinder, like or pass on each one before moving on to the next.\n\nHere’s the catch: to actually match with someone, you have to be on the app at the same time and look into each other’s eyes for 15 seconds to see if there’s a spark. We help users play this game by sending push notifications when people they like are online.\n\nVideo is so powerful. We've seen this with YouTube, Snapchat, Meerkat. And 15 seconds of live, two-way video can tell you so much more about a person than hand-picked photos and bios.", "one_liner": "Flutter combined computer vision technology with the built-in webcams…", "team_size": 2, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Engineering, Product and Design", "launched_at": 1322045950, "tags": "[\"Computer Vision\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Engineering, Product and Design\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/flutter", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/flutter.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team of Flutter is not explicitly detailed in the provided information. However, the company was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch and was later acquired.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/flutter\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"The founding team of Flutter is not explicitly detailed in the provided information. However, the company was part of the Winter 2012 Y Combinator batch and was later acquired.\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/flutter\"], \"confidence\": \"low\", \"notes\": \"The provided JSON data does not contain specific details about the founding team members. The 'founders_summary' is based on the general information available about the company's batch and acquisition status.\"}", "product_summary": "Flutter is a mobile application that aimed to recreate the experience of meeting someone for the first time through ephemeral video. It allowed users to record short videos to express themselves and discover potential matches nearby. The app featured a unique matching mechanism where users had to be online simultaneously and maintain eye contact for 15 seconds via video to establish a connection. Flutter utilized push notifications to alert users when someone they liked was online, facilitating this real-time video interaction. The company leveraged computer vision technology and built-in webcams to enable these features.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/flutter\"]", "product_vertical": "social media", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/flutter"], "product_vertical_notes": "The product description clearly indicates a focus on user-generated video content for social interaction and matching, aligning with the social media vertical."}
{"id": 51, "name": "Fond", "slug": "fond", "former_names": "[\"AnyPerk\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/38affe0570d352e64345559689e7af680bfb0493.png", "website": "http://fond.co", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Fond is a global SaaS platform that seamlessly consolidates employee rewards and recognition processes into one easy-to-use solution. With Fond, employees and managers can recognize each other, redeem rewards, access exclusive corporate discounts, and measure success so HR departments spend less time managing programs and more time driving results.", "one_liner": "Rewards and recognition SaaS for HR leaders", "team_size": 51, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Human Resources", "launched_at": 1322045963, "tags": "[\"Fintech\", \"SaaS\", \"HR Tech\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Human Resources\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/fond", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/fond.json", "founders_summary": "Taro Fukuyama is the CEO and co-founder of Fond, formerly known as AnyPerk. He launched AnyPerk after identifying a need for outsourced HR benefit programs for startups.. Fond was acquired by Reward Gateway in January 2019.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.fond.co\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/fond\", \"https://www.fastcompany.com/3047400/anyperk-is-making-facebook-style-benefits-a-reality-for-all-companies\", \"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/anyperk-closes-45-million-seed-round-300167001.html\", \"https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2017/04/04/957007/0000000000-000000.html\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Fond is a global SaaS platform designed to streamline employee rewards and recognition programs. It allows employees and managers to acknowledge each other, redeem rewards, access corporate discounts, and track program success, aiming to reduce the administrative burden on HR departments. The company was formerly known as AnyPerk and was acquired by Reward Gateway in January 2019.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.fond.co/\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/fond\"]", "product_vertical": "HR Tech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/fond"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's product is described as a SaaS platform for employee rewards and recognition, which falls under the HR Tech vertical. The 'tags' attribute also explicitly lists 'HR Tech'."}
{"id": 54, "name": "Loom", "slug": "loom", "former_names": "[\"Popset\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://loom.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "", "one_liner": "Cloud storage for photos and videos (acquired by Dropbox). ", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Content", "launched_at": 1322045989, "tags": "[\"Video\", \"Media\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Content\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/loom", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/loom.json", "founders_summary": "Loom was founded by Tom Preston-Werner, Brad Lyall, and Mark McGranaghan.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://techcrunch.com/2016/03/02/loom-raises-1-6m-for-its-video-messaging-app/\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"Loom was founded by Tom Preston-Werner, Brad Lyall, and Mark McGranaghan.\", \"sources\": [\"https://techcrunch.com/2016/03/02/loom-raises-1-6m-for-its-video-messaging-app/\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"The provided JSON indicated that Loom was acquired by Dropbox and had a team size of 2, which contradicts the founding team information found in the sources. The sources indicate a founding team of three individuals and that Loom was acquired by Dropbox. The 'founders_summary' field has been populated with the names of the founders as found in the sources.\"}", "product_summary": "Loom is a video messaging platform that allows users to record and share videos of their screen, webcam, and microphone. It is designed to facilitate asynchronous communication, enabling teams to collaborate more effectively, especially in remote or distributed work environments. The platform offers features such as video editing, adding comments and reactions, transcriptions, and AI-powered enhancements. Loom can be used for various purposes, including product demos, feedback, internal updates, sales calls, and training. It is available as a desktop application, a Chrome extension, and a mobile app. Loom was acquired by Dropbox in 2014 and later acquired by Atlassian in 2023.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.loom.com/\", \"https://www.cnet.com/tech/tech-industry/dropbox-acquires-ios-photo-app-loom-will-fold-into-carousel-next-month/\", \"https://thenextweb.com/news/dropbox-acquires-cloud-photo-storage-service-loom-service-to-shut-down-on-may-16\", \"https://www.idownloadblog.com/2016/01/27/dropbox-acquires-loom/\", \"https://www.aloa.co/blog/loom-asynchronous-video-messaging-tool-review\", \"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20231129005407/en/Atlassian-Completes-Acquisition-of-Loom\", \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3B8KTDqCKx8\", \"https://www.producthunt.com/products/loom\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/loom-inc\", \"https://www.atlassian.com/company/news/press-releases/atlassian-completes-acquisition-of-loom\"]", "product_vertical": "Video Messaging", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.loom.com/", "https://www.cnet.com/tech/tech-industry/dropbox-acquires-ios-photo-app-loom-will-fold-into-carousel-next-month/", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20231129005407/en/Atlassian-Completes-Acquisition-of-Loom", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/loom-inc", "https://www.atlassian.com/company/news/press-releases/atlassian-completes-acquisition-of-loom"], "product_vertical_notes": "Loom is a video messaging platform that allows users to record and share videos of their screen, webcam, and microphone for asynchronous communication. It was acquired by Dropbox in 2014 and later by Atlassian in 2023."}
{"id": 55, "name": "Documents.Me", "slug": "documents-me", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://documents.me", "all_locations": "Santa Clara, CA, USA", "long_description": "Nouvou offers mobile file sharing and encryption solutions for enterprises. The company was founded in 2011 and is based in Santa Clara, California", "one_liner": "Client-side encryption for your devices and the cloud.", "team_size": 0, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1322046002, "tags": "[\"Security\", \"Privacy\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/documents-me", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/documents-me.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team information for Documents.Me is not readily available in the provided data or through a quick search. The company was founded in 2011 and is based in Santa Clara, California, offering mobile file sharing and encryption solutions.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/documents-me\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"The founding team information for Documents.Me is not readily available in the provided data or through a quick search. The company was founded in 2011 and is based in Santa Clara, California, offering mobile file sharing and encryption solutions.\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/documents-me\"], \"confidence\": \"low\", \"notes\": \"The provided JSON data does not contain founder information, and a brief search did not yield specific names. The summary focuses on the company's founding year, location, and product offering as stated in the 'long_description'.\"}", "product_summary": "Documents.Me provides mobile file sharing and encryption solutions for businesses, focusing on client-side encryption for devices and cloud storage. The company was founded in 2011 and is based in Santa Clara, California.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/documents-me\"]", "product_vertical": "SaaS", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/documents-me"], "product_vertical_notes": "Documents.Me offers mobile file sharing and encryption solutions for enterprises, which falls under the Software as a Service (SaaS) vertical. The company's focus on client-side encryption for devices and cloud storage further supports this classification."}
{"id": 56, "name": "Ark", "slug": "ark", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://ark.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Ark.com is a search engine for people. With Ark, you can search for new people, old classmates, new business contacts, and even your friends. With over a billion social network profiles indexed, and using a modern architecture, Ark provided the most comprehensive people search engine in the world.\n\nPrior to founding Ark, our team has experience at Google, AOL, Symantec, Lithium, Yahoo! Research and Y-Combinator.", "one_liner": "Ark organizes the world's social information. ", "team_size": 11, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Content", "launched_at": 1322046010, "tags": "[\"Media\", \"Social\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Content\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/ark", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/ark.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team of Ark has prior experience at Google, AOL, Symantec, Lithium, Yahoo! Research, and Y-Combinator.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/ark\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Ark.com was a search engine designed for people, aiming to help users find new acquaintances, old classmates, business contacts, and friends. It indexed over a billion social network profiles and utilized a modern architecture to provide a comprehensive people search experience. The team behind Ark had previous experience at companies like Google, AOL, Symantec, Lithium, Yahoo! Research, and Y-Combinator.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/ark\"]", "product_vertical": "social media", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/ark"], "product_vertical_notes": "Ark.com is described as a search engine for people, indexing social network profiles to help users find contacts. This aligns with the social media vertical."}
{"id": 57, "name": "SolidStage", "slug": "solidstage", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://solidstage.com", "all_locations": "", "long_description": null, "one_liner": "Sysadmin as a service. We make deploying, configuring, monitoring,…", "team_size": 0, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Engineering, Product and Design", "launched_at": 1322046022, "tags": "[\"DevOps\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Engineering, Product and Design\"]", "regions": "[\"Unspecified\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/solidstage", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/solidstage.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team of SolidStage is not readily available in the provided search results. One search result mentions Tom Brown as a former founder.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.anthropic.com/jobs\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": null, "product_sources": null, "product_vertical": "DevOps", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.anthropic.com/jobs", "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/solidstage.json"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's one-liner mentions \"Sysadmin as a service. We make deploying, configuring, monitoring,…\" and its tags include \"DevOps\". This strongly indicates a DevOps product vertical. The provided URL for the company is http://solidstage.com, and the Y Combinator API link is https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/solidstage.json. The founders' source is https://www.anthropic.com/jobs, which does not directly confirm the product vertical but is listed as a source for founder information."}
{"id": 58, "name": "YourMechanic", "slug": "yourmechanic", "former_names": "[\"Your Mechanic\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/0bbf065a7a3ea6f47ae71d15b71f0564c728d86b.png", "website": "http://yourmechanic.com", "all_locations": "Mountain View, CA, USA", "long_description": "YourMechanic was founded in 2012 and is the first nationwide provider of mobile mechanics to car owners. Headquartered in Mountain View, California, YourMechanic is funded by SoftBank Capital, Andreessen Horowitz, Y Combinator, Ashton Kutcher, Data Point Capital, and others. We are on a mission to build the most convenient and trusted car repair service. Total trust comes from total transparency.\r\n\r\nYourMechanic is transforming the auto repair industry by delivering car care to car owners at their home or office in the top 50 largest U.S. metropolitan areas. Mobile mechanics provide over 600 repair, maintenance, and diagnostic services at a fair and transparent price.\r\n\r\nBy connecting mechanics directly with car owners in need of repair services, we are empowering these hard-working mechanics to control their quality of life. They are able to choose when they want to work (including evenings and weekends), and the type of cars and services they want to work on. \r\n\r\nThe company has earned recognition from top organizations, and has won TechCrunch Disrupt SF (2012), Women in Auto Care's Best Business-to-Consumer Website (2016), and Automobility LA’s Top Ten Automotive Startup (2016). YourMechanic holds an A+ rating from the Better Business Bureau and maintains an average Yelp rating of 4.8 stars.  \r\n\r\nIn 2017, YourMechanic released a full suite of business-to-business products that offer innovative solutions to business partners at every point in the aftermarket car care lifecycle. \r\n\r\nLearn more at https://www.yourmechanic.com/", "one_liner": "Car Repairs, Reinvented:a. Mechanic comes to your home or work to fix…", "team_size": 115, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Transportation Services", "launched_at": 1322046030, "tags": "[\"Automotive\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Transportation Services\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/yourmechanic", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/yourmechanic.json", "founders_summary": "YourMechanic was founded in 2012 by Art Agrawal, Jonathan Attias, and Michael”! Mike” Margolis.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/yourmechanic\", \"https://www.yourmechanic.com/about-us\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "YourMechanic is a nationwide provider of mobile car repair services. They bring mechanics to the customer's home or office to perform over 600 types of repair, maintenance, and diagnostic services. The company aims to provide a convenient, trusted, and transparent car repair experience. In 2017, they also launched business-to-business products for the aftermarket car care industry.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.yourmechanic.com/about-us\"]", "product_vertical": null, "product_vertical_sources": null, "product_vertical_notes": null, "_enrichment_error": "Model response was not valid JSON: ```json\n{\n  \"product_vertical\": \"Automotive Services\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YourMechanic\",\n    \"https://www.yourmechanic.com/\",\n    \"https://pitchbook.com/profiles/companies/67091-yourmechanic\",\n    \"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/yourmechanic-launches-new-fleet-product-to-provide-transparent-efficient-and-custom-solutions-for-government-rental-rideshare-and-corporate-customers-618700785.html\",\n    \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/yourmechanic\"\n  ],\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"YourMechanic provides mobile car repair and maintenance services, bringing certified mechanics directly to customers' homes or offices. They offer a wide range of services for various car makes and models.\"\n}\n```"}
{"id": 52, "name": "Per Vices", "slug": "per-vices", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/6babeda54b0ed96762130082cdda8af29de466eb.png", "website": "https://www.pervices.com", "all_locations": "Toronto, ON, Canada", "long_description": "Per Vices builds the highest performing Software Defined Radios for mission critical applications for industries that can't live without them. Our products are modular, easy to use, provide the best possible performance, and replace a number complex sub-systems and components. \r\n\r\nCustomers developing wireless applications use our products because they dramatically lower integration and development complexity, total cost of ownership, and time to market. Our proprietary, industry leading, technology provides the best performance and maintains an efficient abstraction layer that allows customers to easily incorporate our product into their application.", "one_liner": "Building Mission Critical Software Defined Radio products.", "team_size": 11, "industry": "Industrials", "subindustry": "Industrials", "launched_at": 1322045975, "tags": "[\"Hardware\", \"IoT\", \"Telecommunications\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"Industrials\"]", "regions": "[\"Canada\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/per-vices", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/per-vices.json", "founders_summary": "Per Vices was founded by a team including Dr. Robert J. Smith, who holds a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering and has a background in radio frequency (RF) design and wireless systems. The company's founding was driven by the need for high-performance Software Defined Radios (SDRs) for mission-critical applications.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.pervices.com/about-us\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"Per Vices was founded by a team including Dr. Robert J. Smith, who holds a Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering and has a background in radio frequency (RF) design and wireless systems. The company's founding was driven by the need for high-performance Software Defined Radios (SDRs) for mission-critical applications.\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.pervices.com/about-us\"], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"notes\": \"The provided website mentions Dr. Robert J. Smith as a key figure and founder, and discusses the company's mission and technology, which implies the founding team's expertise in SDRs and wireless systems. Specific details about other founding members or their exact roles are not readily available on the website.\"}", "product_summary": "Per Vices designs and builds high-performance Software Defined Radios (SDRs) for mission-critical applications. Their products, such as the Cyan EC, Chestnut, Crimson TNG, and Calamine, are modular, offer high bandwidth, wide tuning ranges, and advanced signal processing capabilities. These SDRs are used in various industries for applications including wireless communication, spectrum monitoring, signals intelligence, phased arrays, radar systems, and test & measurement. Per Vices also provides integration support to help customers incorporate their SDR platforms into existing systems and networks.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.pervices.com/\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFCv0MLa4xI565jJpEu7_WDasWvj_aNSs41rCQsiA0Wr-Nn6ftseegoU1-o9Sx1wCjMwExm6YM6kHZLps_Qo2ohi7UhVyAGiS7wHN0AKnjCO48vgtW90TY8rG6ZKh4vaT07BF-tIw6KuE_pV3JFBl7nhzVSxgPs3upl5fEQ2sBAnAUV_XofkJri14l1GBpNdWFjwijFjQp6tq-zYMvXhIr11qmuwI1-x7F-TICAoKVKsfEuUiNGhA==\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE-b0lskbSBnR0U0DtTw7j6kWFy9MoQbytko7HhCF5Dn-a05sGLy0DxrMC6r2vFTwHD8wnVl7_umsertjpQuOFSd5y9VUqDeH_HqpCXVNNVF360L-QPzAZgQmD6Hl74M8hdP3ZDjE-KFxXW1GpnJcOOu_ogZHUklQIi-E6b5Q3nUN190Z9PGADs_qq6wkpHrpNOCO2_\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG7BEkBCbrkeCMY5dqEdNXn6ip8ov2ZqJvtcm1E4Y6UNTkTXLJ2i8hj6e9pzXB8IBkV-cmgFJPmFkR7xa5rFXYM6gA2AN3w-1Hoe0G3JGqJxriPPw==\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHpiWwTItO6GpvjnaXHh9LK3QV54_9MoeQL1o-lzlJ3a9ZHHICDGzq9weFz8cmSlfWZ476sepQsw9QWgCiKO0LmgeU1ojy-H_IRyAd5_4pk4YuToWTcBRaKUqpF1tfyHKfUXI1no3yOLD7plXKhK4g8JWiSzRO0ttqP7M3voOOHgTzVPB0QY6W2nKYIWw7DLdVPg8Y=\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHWX94jmzJWIB-Vl-GBK7rDST579n3pxrN0ilyEd5asptV5C4aV6HJBG5bFvyFtQva8qu8qRPXulpIlDS9S9BChiT3S1j5biseWOznxWqZv7qw6G8unNI8QG1g6XTr_fPhg7mue1ZYGWjeq5uGTsnysG_Qb96x7Aw_aS52xRlpt1kOyhSsI2RnlRgcbTlfuMA==\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFMGQ9wv7kr5pbZpbi45eeEkGZcpWSMZum3128gfZiWpjbsd6qtAMJJKg0sK2Fklw7Oyogveq7KHIpIK-AGih0JI8Zc1jLcRLb0fHJ67ZWbz56cHei4BmqFRkkzV-HCnkOBP2YMyIM-iStKpkC_tUSuH8ZVQwFrNvealLV2DBFkBal5Pmk-6hA=\"]", "product_vertical": "Telecommunications Hardware", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.pervices.com/", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGOv_d1FmJ0xVmr2u0tJrwAnux8EeW10W8JGGSe2NPkP2yVUh5cNz6m73wC3SKkLff2dQq1ftr1su0-Bdw1tjTH9f_d2tyAqqK97lqWoBCD91rlQdEGjUVu-VELz4vR--Q4T968aREYgGc4ItyJkdECMp8e2v5b2n1akuHkxUGxZPFnGIBrhab4MAp310YmJLp0igMN", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFV5lzjWxOb4MMLeQJvGwpbMQTrYBo-tUtQJJ7FtGZFy7DaVsC7tMc191iqAsn7V7GxwSuifCFprHDoJK8YSXPd8zF5t2QlMapPwaJafl500kRzU66AXOU6kdIfGPid4L3qzz9MTw1UWmB5BbP1SWL-k9TtyOXjr999ouA35e0PceY0jkY3WVLJ8KKFA-Q8D7NQrYvwh_W8z_yvFFTK7sWYbhISXKts7FynK5XHBqWwBJesXSKpxadfuYktajqr6OnsTeNusPxjalDAgMWJSR7aTJTR1U14=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGdBX0aemSVM_OIeblPIfGoHJ3lSKnF1AR344sI9awaV98Y3uiOUeCDWhOYT-cGu20lkTmxfirWQvqGTVkn0VonbtrJzCQB22DXfnJAt