{"id": 77, "name": "Zigfu", "slug": "zigfu", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://breaks.nu", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Zigfu is the easiest way to make and play Kinect apps. Download the plugin, hook up your sensor, and enjoy the future now!", "one_liner": "Layer above Kinect.", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Gaming", "launched_at": 1326789051, "tags": "[\"Augmented Reality\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Gaming\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/zigfu", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zigfu.json", "founders_summary": "Zigfu was a company that developed a plugin to create and play Kinect applications, described as a layer above Kinect.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zigfu.json\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Zigfu offered a plugin that simplified the creation and playback of Kinect applications, aiming to provide an enhanced experience above the standard Kinect functionality.", "product_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zigfu.json\"]", "product_vertical": "gaming", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zigfu.json"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's product summary and industry classification indicate a focus on gaming, specifically related to Kinect applications."}
{"id": 78, "name": "PayDragon", "slug": "paydragon", "former_names": "[\"Paperlinks\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://paperlinks.com", "all_locations": "Los Angeles, CA, USA", "long_description": "Paperlinks' mission is to hyperlink the real world. Currently, Paperlinks fulfills this by providing the ultimate QR code infrastructure for businesses. Paperlinks' solution is end-to-end, providing: a free QR reading app; code generation; a Content Management System for managing code content; and in-house design and print services.", "one_liner": "Hyperlinking the real world.", "team_size": 11, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Food and Beverage", "launched_at": 1326789090, "tags": "[]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Food and Beverage\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/paydragon", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/paydragon.json", "founders_summary": "Hamilton Chan is a serial entrepreneur with experience in law, finance, entertainment, and tech. He has founded or been involved with multiple companies, including PayDragon.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/paydragon\", \"https://nocap.tech/blog/founders/hamilton-chan-paydragon-y-combinator-s11\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "PayDragon, formerly known as Paperlinks, provides QR code infrastructure for businesses. Their solution includes a QR reading app, code generation, a Content Management System for managing code content, and in-house design and print services, aiming to hyperlink the real world.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/paydragon\"]", "product_vertical": "QR Code Technology", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/paydragon"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company provides QR code infrastructure, including a reading app, code generation, and content management. This clearly places it in the QR Code Technology vertical."}
{"id": 75, "name": "Genius", "slug": "genius", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/22f70a1747582c2bb1d490082ec34e1607eca028.png", "website": "https://genius.com", "all_locations": "NY, USA", "long_description": "Genius is the world's biggest encyclopedia of music. Powered by its community, in-house creative team, and the artists themselves, Genius serves music knowledge to over 100 million people each month on Genius.com and everywhere music fans connect across the internet.\r\n\r\nFounded in 2009, Genius began as a platform for annotating rap lyrics. Over the years, it has expanded its mission to include more than hip-hop, and more than just lyrics. Every song has a story that needs to be told, and the biggest names in music—including Frank Ocean, Lorde, and Lin-Manuel Miranda—come to Genius to give the world insight into their art.", "one_liner": "Music Intelligence", "team_size": 101, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Content", "launched_at": 1326789003, "tags": "[\"Music\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Content\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/genius", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/genius.json", "founders_summary": "Genius was founded in August 2009 by Tom Lehman, Ilan Zechory, and Mahbod Moghadam. The company was initially launched as Rap Genius, focusing on annotating rap lyrics. In July 2014, it rebranded to Genius and expanded its scope to include other forms of media. A significant milestone was its acquisition by MediaLab in September 2021 for $80 million.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genius_(company)\", \"https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/lyrics-firm-genius-acquired-for-80m-by-medialab/\", \"https://www.latimes.com/business/story/2021-09-16/genius-lyrics-website-acquired-by-medialab\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Genius is a digital media company that serves as a comprehensive encyclopedia of music knowledge. Initially launched in 2009 as Rap Genius, it focused on annotating rap lyrics. The platform has since expanded its scope to encompass all genres of music and various forms of media, offering insights into songs through annotations by its community, in-house creative team, and artists themselves. Genius reaches over 100 million people monthly through its website, Genius.com, and other online platforms where music fans engage. Notable artists like Frank Ocean, Lorde, and Lin-Manuel Miranda have contributed to the platform to share insights into their work. In September 2021, Genius was acquired by MediaLab for $80 million.", "product_sources": "[\"https://genius.com\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genius_(company)\", \"https://www.musicbusinessworldwide.com/lyrics-firm-genius-acquired-for-80m-by-medialab/\", \"https://www.latimes.com/business/story/2021-09-16/genius-lyrics-website-acquired-by-medialab\"]", "product_vertical": "Music Intelligence", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEXEjztXfKzssV3rw2wCNI7BTol8_e_03JBK3FG1d3D4snIqKSwVuqikrNvfp8ZRs358FaCV3fHieNbQngqL2xcp_Sdog_bFaUacquK62dbmVcFTUMiZ5opiZGdM3-Du0du6f1Wy-ry", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYG7TgBtVn7-d_iXOD6Pzy3VN9yBn0N02DeXW_NR9bjvXvBaOZRHqLjtwD3LcwoTRrR7to1MP-4LhPyd4Q0apeXjd4PtzPK1LEdZ7JPhrlDPL35_XybRyQjLwvEBRyRM2lseB8WxWn75CIrBxXo81wdqQsTToETmMne5ncRH5SWro=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEyJ-0oimORdEsbh_R7WXXIsJ339K7lbnHNay5pU9C9pbvzDes9h7WDO9HbQ-BrYVzRWpJB3YK3yffg597uCCmAysOQ_5sjn9oV7GfntwjHexmyX-jbRQ==", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF-k05wALu0N13cI0ZoyRmS3KTQAiMyK1Gxy2hwG0EjkG5CoU66zhqFwRqCZDROv70RhKfpClfdNVwQ2ALRcZlzHllIZhyXziF6VJjq862enVwSEZUpIo-gK1SEzeWmdmhpLzEryTw6ipNZN77PH71ON0x6", "https://genius.com"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 80, "name": "Debteye", "slug": "debteye", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://debteye.com", "all_locations": "Chicago, IL, USA", "long_description": "Automate credit counseling.", "one_liner": "Automate credit counseling.", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Fintech", "subindustry": "Fintech -> Consumer Finance", "launched_at": 1326789106, "tags": "[\"Fintech\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Fintech\", \"Consumer Finance\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/debteye", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/debteye.json", "founders_summary": "Debteye was co-founded by Paul Zhang and John Sun. Paul Zhang later co-founded Avant and served as its CTO. John Sun also co-founded Avant.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF3DCGSu3anY7geRny845Wj7IHbNDf4Nv4LayjJJWRdToJKGdiHoyQp-Obh2DZrgoQ-U4N-DENoLpqmenfFEfes8-LnD2itvV8tfY7w1BWmT5LWhOgcQEMw2L7-amsvHSXaBKLSmxlKNA==\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHdPpZYfTZbgZ2g_8nfafIYd0Z6j_qovCjHzwAYZHRlP5zGxyoahqWEHCisO3W1tvHeCMONwhaEu86ZVNn0ZRuUi1oaiIoJVXG0-BvbIuTByvDjIr2c1KaKH_V6ZFMNb_XEp0W1Xqg5w6Ar-RoV4eZfqbyqd4pFVsIFUQMnSYiwIK7OXHNQ85MyX5JHOIm_w8Akv6V_56FhqYU5AiposkniQhzuzALwGaFVcVV-giRtvm3kTQ-RDrkKQcw=\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE2EbzT2K-AMUktP9dmWeBnYSO678aUGtHvxFYUsoi9bY5_iNhBQEgRoMaU7rroXwaPx2uj9q8SFhc8Rvps_5V5ZY9YF-AHcdK0N7t-AieOZ0EKw0tZykuZQKMCsDo4vEBL19sa4MJ_ZA==\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFUV41gKIieY6N6O-Pk8HWTx2D1m8fCVHmW8KpUMeNSmluVxmFxjptECMBWwdnjdDI28TlPkSnXIuKV_jUCfVSBAw07g7rpwWlFMgzqYxQUZpYFBB4cdXWgwXOh4SRwyWxPRT6p8KN9\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Debteye aimed to automate credit counseling by helping users fill out pre-generated forms for debt management plans and providing scripts for communicating with creditors. The service, which was free at launch and planned to charge a monthly fee, utilized Yodlee to scrape financial records. While the founders were certified credit counselors, the company faced skepticism regarding its ability to truly automate debt renegotiation through bank APIs. Debteye was acquired and its founders later co-founded Avant.", "product_sources": "[\"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFQfCrO6Lm5Sz_N3uzVWCAip0DAVwSK0FYoNdW_NL-V5oDklXCgnpheLyLq35g3rHEWQyqsg-YI9paZhdAvr3I7UyTzXxKsLZAue4OS-xL9Q_Hz-bn3xOdcMx8GP3-j4wOtsBTAGUKZ4rpWGxmaeVVUXE5s5wd9ecmYgSy_XhAMpQ10zBvHSqumL2XlLKK3dj6dga24nJCUIh813LuARNIlijfDe9fsUw6SnQ==\", \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE7vufmC_8QvYyk1i40eQxnmwqAAWr1U8omuBIfXio1Fcr68PFUBT_2gV3tAokAg_myqvSA3nxXnV4vgLRRDH6LXh7j8JbvskOCEHDiu1kVEZGNIZcCOk327Ufv6gbJ9c_dz1kzdJCivQ==\"]", "product_vertical": "Fintech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/debteye.json"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's industry is explicitly listed as 'Fintech' and its sub-industry as 'Fintech -> Consumer Finance'. The product summary also details its focus on automating credit counseling and debt management plans, which falls under the fintech umbrella."}
{"id": 79, "name": "Aisle50", "slug": "aisle50", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://aisle50.com", "all_locations": "Chicago, IL, USA", "long_description": "Aisle50 came out of the summer 2011 class at Y Combinator, the Silicon Valley accelerator.  Aisle50 builds CPG and retailer campaigns aimed to get both banner and brand incremental shoppers, bigger share and valuable brand messaging to consumers.\n\nOur product has a two-year track record of producing baskets that are 30% larger for our retailers.  We also give our retailer partners incremental trips that, in the past, they would have lost to competitors.  Aisle50 content, because much of it is in the form of offers that are paid for through Web or Mobile, compel the consumer to head to the store sooner rather than later.  \n\nEverybody wins: We drive trips to stores, new customers to CPGs and big discounts to consumers.", "one_liner": "Grocery deals.", "team_size": 11, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Home and Personal", "launched_at": 1326789097, "tags": "[\"Grocery\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Home and Personal\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/aisle50", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/aisle50.json", "founders_summary": "Aisle50 was co-founded by Chris Steiner and Riley Scott. George Korsnick also served as a founder and CTO.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/aisle50\", \"https://techli.com/2013/08/aisle50-secures-2-6-million/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Aisle50 is a company that develops consumer packaged goods (CPG) and retailer campaigns designed to attract incremental shoppers, increase market share, and deliver valuable brand messaging to consumers. Their product has a two-year track record of increasing retailer basket sizes by 30% and driving incremental trips that might otherwise be lost to competitors. Aisle50's offers, often funded through web or mobile platforms, incentivize consumers to visit stores sooner.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/aisle50\"]", "product_vertical": null, "product_vertical_sources": null, "product_vertical_notes": null, "_enrichment_error": "Model response was not valid JSON: ```json\n{\n  \"product_vertical\": \"e-commerce\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/aisle50\",\n    \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/aisle50/profile\",\n    \"https://builtin.com/company/aisle50\"\n  ],\n  \"confidence\": \"high\",\n  \"notes\": \"Aisle50's product involves selling digital offers for CPGs directly to consumers, who then redeem them at grocery stores. This aligns with an e-commerce vertical, specifically focusing on digital coupons and online-to-offline retail.\"\n}\n```"}
{"id": 82, "name": "Streak", "slug": "streak", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/34b83cec1f2ebdc9cb570890712a93e354509aec.png", "website": "http://streak.com", "all_locations": "Remote", "long_description": "Streak is the only CRM integrated entirely within your Gmail inbox, and works alongside all your other G Suite applications. It can be used to track any business process including sales, partnerships, support, hiring, deal flow, and much more. Streak also includes a powerful set of email tools including email tracking, send later, snoozing, mail merge, and more.", "one_liner": "Streak transforms Gmail into a powerful CRM", "team_size": 35, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Sales", "launched_at": 1326789125, "tags": "[\"SaaS\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 1, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Sales\"]", "regions": "[\"Remote\", \"Fully Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/streak", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/streak.json", "founders_summary": "Streak was founded in 2011 by Aleem Mawani, a former Google product manager, and Omar Ismail.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.streak.com/\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Streak_(company)\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Streak is a Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system that is fully integrated within the Gmail inbox. It functions alongside other G Suite applications and can be utilized to manage various business processes such as sales, partnerships, support, hiring, and deal flow. Additionally, Streak offers email tools including email tracking, scheduled sending, snoozing, and mail merge capabilities.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.streak.com/\"]", "product_vertical": "CRM", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.streak.com/"], "product_vertical_notes": "Streak is described as a CRM integrated within Gmail, managing business processes like sales and support."}
{"id": 83, "name": "Science Exchange", "slug": "science-exchange", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/0db3228fbd884724c2ad75aeac20b60376478518.png", "website": "https://www.scienceexchange.com/", "all_locations": "Palo Alto, CA, USA; Remote", "long_description": "Science Exchange powers R&D outsourcing for the world’s top life sciences companies. Our marketplace gives scientists access to the innovation and research they need and our platform fully automates R&D outsourcing from source to pay so scientists can focus on what they love—science.", "one_liner": "Powering scientific outsourcing", "team_size": 50, "industry": "Healthcare", "subindustry": "Healthcare -> Healthcare Services", "launched_at": 1326789132, "tags": "[\"SaaS\", \"Health Tech\", \"Biotech\", \"Enterprise\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Healthcare\", \"Healthcare Services\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Fully Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/science-exchange", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/science-exchange.json", "founders_summary": "Science Exchange was founded in 2011 by Elizabeth Iorns, Ryan Abbott, and Dan Knox.. Elizabeth Iorns, a PhD-trained cancer biologist, was inspired to start the company after experiencing difficulties finding collaborators and providers for her research.. The company participated in the Y Combinator startup accelerator program in the summer of 2011.. Notable milestones include the launch of a program with antibodies-online.com to validate research antibodies in 2013, and a partnership with PLOS in 2012 to launch the Reproducibility Initiative.. In 2016, Science Exchange raised $25 million in Series B funding, followed by $28 million in Series C funding in 2017, and an additional $20 million in 2019.. In 2024, Science Exchange was acquired by Waud Capital Partners.. In March 2025, Science Exchange acquired HappiLabs..", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.scienceexchange.com/\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_Exchange\", \"https://www.waudcapital.com/news/waud-capital-partners-acquires-science-exchange/\", \"https://www.pehub.com/waud-capital-snaps-up-health-tech-firm-science-exchange/\", \"https://www.citybiz.com/news/waud-capital-partners-acquires-science-exchange/\", \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/science-exchange/funding-and-investors\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/science-exchange\", \"https://bowerycapital.com/blog/from-the-front-lines-elizabeth-iorns-science-exchange/\", \"https://blog.ted.com/speaker/elizabeth-iorns/\", \"https://www.auckland.ac.nz/en/alumni/connect-and-engage/alumni-in-the-news/2017/03/elizabeth-iorns.html\", \"https://www.scienceexchange.com/blog/say-hello-to-the-next-evolution-of-science-exchange\", \"https://www.scienceexchange.com/blog/science-exchange-unveils-supplier-orchestration-platform-for-life-sciences-organizations\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Science Exchange is a cloud-based R&D marketplace and a supplier orchestration platform designed for life sciences companies. It offers a comprehensive solution for R&D outsourcing by automating the entire process from sourcing and purchasing to supplier management and payment processing. The platform provides access to a network of thousands of scientific suppliers and services, streamlining workflows, ensuring compliance, and accelerating research timelines. Key features include a unified marketplace experience, automated guided buying, customizable workflows, and AI-powered payment processing.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.scienceexchange.com/\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_Exchange\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/science-exchange\", \"https://www.scienceexchange.com/blog/science-exchange-unveils-supplier-orchestration-platform-for-life-sciences-organizations\"]", "product_vertical": "Healthtech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.scienceexchange.com/", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_Exchange", "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/science-exchange"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's product description and industry classification clearly indicate it operates within the Healthtech vertical, focusing on R&D outsourcing for life sciences companies."}
{"id": 81, "name": "Proxino", "slug": "proxino", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://proxino.com", "all_locations": "Palo Alto, CA, USA", "long_description": "Proxino is a cloud platform for monitoring and debugging client-side JavaScript.", "one_liner": "Javascript proxy.", "team_size": null, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1326789117, "tags": "[\"Developer Tools\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/proxino", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/proxino.json", "founders_summary": "Proxino was founded by Muzzammil (MZ) Zaveri and Ethan Fast.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/proxino\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Proxino is a cloud platform designed for monitoring and debugging client-side JavaScript applications. It acts as a JavaScript proxy, allowing developers to observe and troubleshoot their code in real-time.", "product_sources": "[\"https://proxino.com/\"]", "product_vertical": "Developer Tools", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/proxino"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's product summary explicitly states it is a cloud platform for monitoring and debugging client-side JavaScript, and the industry/subindustry tags also point to infrastructure and developer tools."}
{"id": 84, "name": "PhoneSys", "slug": "phonesys", "former_names": "[\"Pingm\", \"PhoneSys (Pingm)\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/97ac2d1f2ee3d7797ec3d2c94a674d1bedc1494d.png", "website": "http://pingm.net", "all_locations": "Mountain View, CA, USA", "long_description": "Formerly Pingm.", "one_liner": "The Phone System for Sales Teams.", "team_size": 4, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1326789148, "tags": "[\"Sales\", \"CRM\", \"Telecommunications\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/phonesys", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/phonesys.json", "founders_summary": "David Dolphin and Patrick O'Doherty are the founders of PhoneSys.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/phonesys\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "PhoneSys, formerly known as Pingm, offers a phone system specifically designed for sales teams. It integrates with CRM functionalities and falls under the B2B Infrastructure industry, with tags including Sales, CRM, and Telecommunications.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/phonesys\"]", "product_vertical": "Telecommunications", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/phonesys"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's one-liner, tags, and product summary all indicate a focus on telecommunications for sales teams."}
{"id": 85, "name": "Quartzy", "slug": "quartzy", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/4040613ddc6090974d404ee7a77c5ebad60a1e10.png", "website": "https://www.quartzy.com", "all_locations": "Hayward, CA, USA", "long_description": "The world’s No. 1 lab management platform. We help scientists easily organize orders, manage inventory, and save money.", "one_liner": "Marketplace for life science supplies.", "team_size": 100, "industry": "Healthcare", "subindustry": "Healthcare -> Healthcare IT", "launched_at": 1326789155, "tags": "[\"SaaS\", \"B2B\", \"E-commerce\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"Healthcare\", \"Healthcare IT\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/quartzy", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/quartzy.json", "founders_summary": "Quartzy was co-founded in 2011 by Jayant Kulkarni and Adam Regelmann, who met at Columbia University as PhD students. Kulkarni serves as CEO and Regelmann as COO. Ajoy Sojan is also listed as a co-founder and CTO. Notable milestones include the launch of the Quartzy Shop in early 2018, an online marketplace for lab supplies, which by then offered access to over three million products and a community of over 1,000 suppliers. By July 2022, Quartzy served over 300,000 scientists and had two fulfillment centers, one in Hayward, California, and another in Pine Brook, New Jersey.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartzy\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/quartzy\", \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/quartzy/profiles/founders-and-board-of-directors\", \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/quartzy/profiles/company-profile\", \"https://zippia.com/company/quartzy-1647000000/executives\", \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8_Q_0_0_0_0\", \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8_Q_0_0_0_0\", \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=8_Q_0_0_0_0\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Quartzy is a lab management platform designed to help scientists organize orders, manage inventory, and reduce costs. It also functions as an online marketplace for life science supplies, offering access to a wide range of products from numerous suppliers. The platform serves over 300,000 scientists and operates fulfillment centers in California and New Jersey.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.quartzy.com\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartzy\"]", "product_vertical": "Healthtech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quartzy", "https://www.quartzy.com", "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/quartzy"], "product_vertical_notes": "Quartzy is described as a lab management platform and a marketplace for life science supplies, serving scientists and research organizations. This aligns with the Healthtech vertical, encompassing software and services for the healthcare and life sciences industries."}
{"id": 87, "name": "Cryptoseal", "slug": "cryptoseal", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/f01716372f6f7ee7618920ade7a25141ed7d5274.png", "website": "http://cryptoseal.com", "all_locations": "Mountain View, CA, USA", "long_description": "CryptoSeal provides Virtual Private Networks (VPNs) as a service.", "one_liner": "Server key management, VPN as a Service, Privacy VPN.  Sold to…", "team_size": 3, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1326789171, "tags": "[\"Cloud Workload Protection\", \"DevSecOps\", \"Next-gen Network Security\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cryptoseal", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/cryptoseal.json", "founders_summary": "CryptoSeal provides Virtual Private Networks (VPNs) as a service.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cryptoseal\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "CryptoSeal offers Virtual Private Networks (VPNs) as a service, focusing on server key management and privacy.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/cryptoseal\"]", "product_vertical": "VPN / Network Security", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.zdnet.com/article/cloudflare-acquires-vpn-service-cryptoseal-shuts-it-down/", "https://techcrunch.com/2014/06/18/cloudflare-acquires-cryptoseal-to-bolster-its-security-offerings/"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company provided Virtual Private Networks (VPNs) as a service, and was acquired by Cloudflare for its technology. The product vertical is clearly defined as VPN and network security."}
{"id": 88, "name": "Segment", "slug": "segment", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/99f5abd1f15fa4ca4394b5781c98d8ff23db6f7b.png", "website": "http://segment.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Segment is one place to collect customer data and send it to your tools for analytics, marketing automation, and raw data access with SQL. Implement all of your event tracking with Segment’s single API instead of wrangling a new API for every new tool or database. Segment's integrations let you send your data to hundreds of tools and databases.", "one_liner": "Software and APIs to collect, clean, and control customer data.", "team_size": 550, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Analytics", "launched_at": 1326789181, "tags": "[\"SaaS\", \"B2B\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 1, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Analytics\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/segment", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/segment.json", "founders_summary": "Segment was founded in 2011 by Calvin French Owen, Peter Reinhardt, Ilya Volodarsky, and Ian Taylor. The company was acquired by Twilio on October 9, 2020, for $3.2 billion. In 2020, Deloitte named Segment as one of North America's fastest-growing technology companies.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/segment/140000/company-profile\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/segment\", \"https://www.accel.com/companies/segment\", \"https://ltse.com/insights/qa-segment-founder-and-ceo-peter-reinhardt-talks-product-market-fit-fundraising-and-sales\", \"https://growfers.com/segment-unicorn-status-customer-data-platform\", \"https://mailchimp.com/resources/business-milestones/\", \"https://www.shopify.com/blog/business-milestones\", \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AUZIYQHfOZQ\", \"https://segment.com/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Segment is a customer data platform that provides software and APIs to collect, clean, and control customer data. It allows businesses to consolidate customer data from various sources into a single place and then send it to other tools for analytics, marketing automation, and raw data access. Segment's single API simplifies event tracking, eliminating the need to integrate with individual tools and databases.", "product_sources": "[\"https://segment.com/\"]", "product_vertical": "Customer Data Platform", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://segment.com/"], "product_vertical_notes": "Segment's product summary clearly describes it as a customer data platform that collects, cleans, and controls customer data, sending it to various tools for analytics and marketing automation."}
{"id": 86, "name": "Codecademy", "slug": "codecademy", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/ee26c3b11a260e7a045f68b47d8c804b306db89f.png", "website": "http://codecademy.com", "all_locations": "New York, NY, USA", "long_description": "Working professionals are experiencing their jobs changing amidst the rise of technology and automation threatens over 800 million jobs. At the same time, software is eating the world, disrupting every major industry, and creating millions of new technology jobs that companies are eager to fill. This is the skills gap. Our mission is closing it.\r\n\r\nIn 2011, we changed the face of education by creating free interactive coding courses explored by over 45 million people. As we look to the future, we're focused on helping anyone get the skills they need for the jobs they want.  We aim to bridge the gap: between companies and the workforce, people and their dream jobs. Join one of the most dynamic technology companies in New York that is changing the way the world learns.\r\n\r\nHeadquartered in New York City, our team is filled with highly curious diverse individuals whose backgrounds span tech and education. Our team is passionate about our mission: helping people get the skills they need for the jobs they want. We seek transparency, thrive on feedback, value teamwork, love evolving and never forget it's people first. We enjoy catered lunches together, company outings, guest speakers and long walks on the beach.", "one_liner": "The leading online learning platform for technical skills.", "team_size": 225, "industry": "Education", "subindustry": "Education", "launched_at": 1326789163, "tags": "[\"Education\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 1, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Education\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/codecademy", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/codecademy.json", "founders_summary": "Codecademy was founded in August 2011 by Zach Sims and Ryan Bubinski. Sims, who was a student at Columbia University, dropped out to focus on launching the venture. Bubinski also graduated from Columbia University in 2011.\n\nNotable milestones for Codecademy include its launch in 2011, quickly gaining traction with over 200,000 users in its first weekend and reaching 1 million users by the end of that year. In 2013, Codecademy was recognized as the \"Best Education Startup\" at the Crunchie Awards. The platform launched its first iOS app, \"Hour of Code,\" in December 2013. In August 2017, Codecademy launched its paid \"Pro\" subscription service. A significant milestone occurred in December 2021 when Skillsoft acquired Codecademy for approximately $525 million.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zach_Sims\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codecademy\", \"https://www.justgrind.com/podcast/2021/05/zach-sims-codecademy/\", \"https://canvasbusinessmodel.com/codecademy-history/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Codecademy is an online learning platform that offers interactive coding courses. It was founded in August 2011 with the mission of closing the skills gap by providing individuals with the technical skills needed for in-demand technology jobs. The platform initially offered free interactive coding courses and has since expanded to include a paid \"Pro\" subscription service. Codecademy aims to bridge the gap between companies and the workforce, and between people and their dream jobs.", "product_sources": "[\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codecademy\", \"https://canvasbusinessmodel.com/codecademy-history/\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/codecademy\"]", "product_vertical": "EdTech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Codecademy", "https://canvasbusinessmodel.com/codecademy-history/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/codecademy", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHg-GfGZVAuRoBHUac651syrWG7FnMthE8h65_4tXFb8ue3ZWrz8XmvTywwv0drfs3WFIDUFzRhN73BYKuyqXxMUVcjb54GpQvIjegs3kcp5nCwZkmk9aUQMGNkk87jJjCsbM8rurAFPU2ZZtb7xOCOe-qa4_ajT-UEvrSrQWis5MyUmkzVJ0Rmaw=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEHARU2-o86j5x-AueUcnTo5ife7Ir4N3nmuDjgJnmjlpm9nVGHKkb4ophHAfU_5vLGB-qP-GdnlqL66MUm-we27Gk27KsKg1clrfsuDdMgcNhEX4TzTXZ6sTFxkhitMSuRuh6lfsRwzG89G8LjL1BjExdHH1Of"], "product_vertical_notes": "Codecademy is an online learning platform that offers interactive coding courses, fitting the EdTech (Education Technology) vertical. Its primary focus is on providing technical skills education through an online platform, utilizing a freemium model with both free and paid subscription options."}
{"id": 90, "name": "AgileMD", "slug": "agilemd", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/809b12f827ff69a7f32abee89d407ac3eac9359d.png", "website": "https://agilemd.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA; Remote", "long_description": "At AgileMD, we are building the most advanced real-time predictive analytics and clinical algorithms platform for hospitals. Our cloud-based engine helps thousands of doctors and nurses around the country make medical decisions, so that every patient receives the highest quality and value of care based on the latest medical knowledge and data.", "one_liner": "Predictive analytics and clinical pathways for hospitals ", "team_size": 18, "industry": "Healthcare", "subindustry": "Healthcare -> Healthcare IT", "launched_at": 1326789206, "tags": "[\"Machine Learning\", \"Healthcare\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"Healthcare\", \"Healthcare IT\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Fully Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/agilemd", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/agilemd.json", "founders_summary": "AgileMD was founded by Kurt Ericson and Borna Safabakhsh. Borna Safabakhsh also serves as the CEO of the company. Dana Edelson, MD, is also a co-founder and the Chief Medical Officer.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/agilemd/profile\", \"https://www.uchicagomed.org/about/news/2024/06/agilemd-fda-nod\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "AgileMD provides a cloud-based platform that offers real-time predictive analytics and clinical algorithms for hospitals. Their engine assists doctors and nurses in making medical decisions to ensure patients receive high-quality, value-based care informed by the latest medical knowledge and data.", "product_sources": "[\"https://agilemd.com\"]", "product_vertical": "Healthtech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://agilemd.com"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's product summary clearly states they provide a platform for hospitals with real-time predictive analytics and clinical algorithms, directly aligning with the healthtech vertical."}
{"id": 91, "name": "Clerky", "slug": "clerky", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/0413dbdb2293e4b9ea1ccbeb3fd25e23c7e07440.png", "website": "https://www.clerky.com", "all_locations": "Palo Alto, CA, USA; Burlingame, CA, USA; Remote", "long_description": "Clerky builds software to make legal paperwork easier for startups and their attorneys.  From formation to fundraising to hiring - everything a startup needs.  Thousands of top startups use Clerky to get legal paperwork done safely and efficiently.", "one_liner": "Makes legal paperwork easy for startups and their attorneys.", "team_size": 15, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Legal", "launched_at": 1700550246, "tags": "[\"Documents\", \"Legal\", \"LegalTech\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Legal\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Fully Remote\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/clerky", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/clerky.json", "founders_summary": "Clerky was founded by Chris Field and Darby Wong. Both founders are former startup attorneys who previously worked at Orrick, Herrington & Sutcliffe LLP in Silicon Valley. They observed firsthand the legal challenges startups faced due to subpar online services or DIY approaches, which inspired them to create Clerky.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/clerky\", \"https://clerky.com/about\", \"https://www.forbes.com/sites/frederickallen/2025/04/18/why-startup-founders-love-this-company/\", \"https://international-finance.com/clerky-review-startup-legal-services/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Clerky provides software designed to simplify legal paperwork for startups and their legal counsel. Their platform aims to streamline processes from company formation and fundraising to hiring, offering a comprehensive solution for startup legal needs. Thousands of startups reportedly utilize Clerky for secure and efficient legal documentation.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.clerky.com\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/clerky\"]", "product_vertical": "LegalTech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.clerky.com", "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/clerky"], "product_vertical_notes": "Clerky provides software to simplify legal paperwork for startups, aligning with the LegalTech vertical."}
{"id": 94, "name": "Dubjoy", "slug": "dubjoy", "former_names": "[\"DoubleRecall\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/5bde29500d01b2d805112b253770eaf004e9a0dd.png", "website": "http://dubjoy.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Dubjoy makes it easy for anyone to translate and voice-over any video.\r\n\r\nBusinesses that produce or host a lot of video content use Dubjoy to grow faster and go global.\r\n\r\nPeople who speak at least 2 languages are able to earn some extra cash or create a job for themselves.", "one_liner": "Dubjoy translates and voice-overs your video to any language", "team_size": 2, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Marketing", "launched_at": 1326789254, "tags": "[\"Video\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Marketing\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/dubjoy", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/dubjoy.json", "founders_summary": "Y Combinator is the largest and only investor in Dubjoy, having participated in their Seed round in 2011.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/dubjoy/funding-rounds-investors\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Dubjoy is a platform that allows users to translate and voice-over any video. It is designed for businesses that produce or host a lot of video content, enabling them to expand their reach globally. It also offers opportunities for individuals who are bilingual to earn income or create employment by providing translation and voice-over services.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/dubjoy\"]", "product_vertical": "Video Translation and Dubbing", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/dubjoy", "https://dubwise.ai/video-translation", "https://ai-studios.com/ai-dubbing", "https://dubly.ai/", "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RaskAI"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 89, "name": "Citus Data", "slug": "citus-data", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/202e7e02db190c7ab3eef78d63f9fe5d31e43275.png", "website": "http://citusdata.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA; Istanbul, Istanbul, Turkey; Amsterdam, NH, Netherlands", "long_description": "The amount of time businesses spend on their databases is altogether too much time. Citus is fixing this problem.\r\n\r\nCitus is worry-free Postgres. Built to scale out, Citus is an extension to Postgres that is available as open source, as enterprise software that can be run on-prem or on any cloud, and as a fully-managed database as a service. Whether you have a multi-tenant application that needs to scale out, or you need performance for your real-time analytics customers, with Citus, you can focus on your app—not your database.\r\n\r\nFounded in 2011, Citus Data is venture backed by Khosla Ventures and Data Collective. Citus is a Y Combinator alumnus and has offices in San Francisco’s SoMa district and Istanbul, Turkey.  \r\n\r\nAt Citus, we make it simple to scale out Postgres. \r\n\r\nCitus Data online: www.citusdata.com\r\nDocumentation: docs.citusdata.com\r\nGitHub: github.com/citusdata/citus", "one_liner": "Real-time. Big data. PostgreSQL", "team_size": 45, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1326789195, "tags": "[\"Open Source\", \"Big Data\", \"Databases\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"Turkey\", \"Netherlands\", \"America / Canada\", \"Middle East and North Africa\", \"Europe\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/citus-data", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/citus-data.json", "founders_summary": "Citus Data was founded by Ozgun Erdogan, Umut Uyar, and Timur Akkaya.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.citusdata.com/about/\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/citus-data\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Citus is an extension to PostgreSQL that allows businesses to scale out their databases. It is available as open-source software, an enterprise solution for on-premises or cloud deployment, and a fully managed database-as-a-service. Citus aims to simplify database scaling for applications requiring multi-tenant architecture or high performance for real-time analytics.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.citusdata.com/\"]", "product_vertical": "Databases", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHRqNk_TeeT1V1Mfe0KISdN2qU6yErdvHKc-YPDvXxiTnWWaXRNjFLX7ds442UAbR2A_gZXiKIodjUlBMTfAMcF5d5rpWhP85c298Z7rGEeAIyBAx7ECUL8q0sPGk7BjeBnuZtj2AhEjiD6fFg6GkxMR3pbviQKZC2yXMSKvO3OSwMcH0k=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFWMirM6AXQdO9kDkJFyV2mN7N9pnmYNvXYX_Er2608Eb308N1nj2CERP1Eme0mM4QgizIAEqY09Tys3jh8gK0ACc17YaGx6pTQ5KTKQGPZONE_p7Dh", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGxkhKxEsDr5P4H-K_CtTUf8C65OcXMQUdNrRFM73kshisoHVMgd0ytMutgvsCJmpWHuAsMfFOqWGDrZD0WCnrJjNx7OdvXkBc9_W0R1Hg32CusZoL-e58F-6w-p6Q=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGhNKWoZ82FqEdTkHX9h-edOJj8HeyBRL3xOzOHrIxj0kXJWumAcYKDO4zrJ1XGynBW8CbREUctRPfN3wlKB91GH7Lf80e_9kGhTbknU20s6hhOhSrSrgUc60VnwSP3Tcq2QqTk4DWW9gLv9p1iwCEoEFxHfPnuxuDx-UdrH6nciOB7sBsFCA==", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGzLHcLvEzSRvQyHtODm__a43TAHGkGp_9uoYnX509pKZOPsgYdg9FvaM2AhewSNrTaRSRrutPUWLSdscp78MSbjrGbCPnJ1JsHBxTKOh6YCyGZtRtX_REiFimqOBaOpZzRG-cXhob-CJ6KAMXgpGm5DpJ1p2ahWF2z505uon4GoUZg6Ja4PPLHuko83w=="], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 92, "name": "Quad", "slug": "quad", "former_names": "[\"CampusCred\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/97b65f8dea0502efd7643266c7f38485fe09a254.png", "website": "http://thequad.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Quad is where college students get things done.\r\n \r\nToday, over 41% of students drop out, 1 in 3 struggle with time management, and 45% end up underemployed because most solutions are ineffective for the modern student. We built Quad to fix this.\r\n\r\nQuad enables students to automatically keep track of their daily coursework, chat with their classmates, and get help - all in one mobile platform. Our proprietary technology transforms assignment information traditionally locked inside the syllabus into dynamic and structured data students utilize daily. \r\n\r\nWe believe that technology with the power to engage students on a daily basis has the ability to fundamentally improve student outcomes.", "one_liner": "Quad is where college students get things done.", "team_size": 12, "industry": "Education", "subindustry": "Education", "launched_at": 1326789223, "tags": "[\"Education\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Education\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/quad", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/quad.json", "founders_summary": "Quad was founded by a team including CEO Jordan Wong, CTO Ben Yu, and CPO Alex Tan. The company was part of the Summer 2011 Y Combinator batch.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/quad.json\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Quad is a mobile platform designed to help college students manage their academic lives. It automatically tracks coursework, facilitates communication with classmates, and provides assistance, aiming to improve student outcomes by addressing issues like time management and underemployment. The platform transforms syllabus information into dynamic, structured data for daily student use.", "product_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/quad.json\"]", "product_vertical": null, "product_vertical_sources": null, "product_vertical_notes": null, "_enrichment_error": "Model response was not valid JSON: ```json\n{\n \"product_vertical\": \"EdTech\",\n \"sources\": [\n  \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/quad\",\n  \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGDJGvcxCPD6EFDPw64j6J5LcDAQ5Xv12bk27OPIV7C93KMhHDUEQI_VzAien66ghVNj1Ds9B2TZ5SDowS3Fn6bwGh5SuGWgjqd4qzwoADtNQWCOT5WGziirJH5mRAy7Vg_JmafNg==\",\n  \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGKdRghYlpqRlkm9wGBe-1wC7P4oaOnSl4rsVr9nhyFEgiWTyptJ6WNnl_PKRES4CCk5QU8kXCR_uY6shMpEhdGmeTNUY0QI3XHy-YL1czOJdZAlcKdWegFlJaNFMkwEe-xWM_o5Wh4tyT70T2RVKE=\",\n  \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGr2BtCT5gwmpJIR-mcoiJUUWIpx-ybAZ-2LbpgHvMCiaf2mkgfkTCUT8jenDnBwV1BPdraUT0T78YkybHhZ7Jq7e3Em3YGJfPha6wZdcaffM50mafXhBdOOggJbrle9iAmRb5Dnjk=\",\n  \"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFor3g2k-l2EsKc5WdeNNys0ZJEOhF9wHX6PNRj65rZJ2FWtSVUCKRjtsOCLdUT_pvMpB3oY-pLLxqEmyqVeaapqeR5r5FDFY0wakuMBidxj3G-JowW8qJfrKSZ6oxR4u-Z_GjEDCE=\"\n ],\n \"confidence\": \"high\",\n \"notes\": \"Quad is an EdTech company that provides a mobile platform for college students to manage coursework, communicate with classmates, and get help. It aims to improve student outcomes by transforming assignment information into dynamic data.\"\n}\n```"}
{"id": 96, "name": "Realm", "slug": "realm", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/e7c0efa8c2a26fb6420ba78e65ca6bed2a565d94.png", "website": "http://realm.io", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA; Copenhagen, Denmark", "long_description": "Realm (formerly tight.db) is a mobile database that enables its users to develop applications faster, develop applications that are fast, and craft amazing user experiences. Realm is a replacement for SQLite & Core Data. It can save users thousands of lines of code & weeks of work, and lets them craft amazing new user experiences. It is a Y Combinator company, headquartered in San Francisco.", "one_liner": "Better data structures = no DB.", "team_size": 51, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1326789275, "tags": "[]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"Denmark\", \"America / Canada\", \"Europe\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/realm", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/realm.json", "founders_summary": "Realm was founded by a team including Alexander Stig, Marc Porcaro, and Bjarne Vest.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/realm-io\", \"https://www.linkedin.com/company/realm-io\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/person/alexander-stig\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/person/marc-porcaro\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/person/bjarne-vest\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Realm is a mobile database designed to help developers build applications faster and create better user experiences. It serves as an alternative to SQLite and Core Data, aiming to reduce coding time and effort. The company was a Y Combinator participant and is headquartered in San Francisco.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/realm\"]", "product_vertical": "Developer Tools", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/realm"], "product_vertical_notes": "Realm is described as a mobile database that helps developers build applications faster, positioning it within the developer tools vertical."}
{"id": 95, "name": "Zenbox", "slug": "zenbox", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://zenboxapp.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Zenbox is a browser extension that connects all of your SaaS services.Open an email, and Zenbox pulls in your customer information from dozens of services right into the sidebar.", "one_liner": "Brings dozens of SaaS's (Mailchimp, Stripe, Shopify, Salesforce,…", "team_size": 2, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Productivity", "launched_at": 1326789268, "tags": "[\"SaaS\", \"Productivity\", \"Email\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Productivity\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/zenbox", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zenbox.json", "founders_summary": "Zenbox is a browser extension that connects all of your SaaS services, pulling customer information from various services into the sidebar when you open an email.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zenbox.json\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Zenbox is a browser extension designed to integrate various SaaS services. It functions by displaying customer information from multiple platforms directly in the sidebar when a user opens an email. This aims to streamline workflows by providing relevant data contextually within the email client.", "product_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zenbox.json\"]", "product_vertical": "Productivity Software", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/zenbox.json"], "product_vertical_notes": "Zenbox is described as a browser extension that connects SaaS services and pulls customer information into the sidebar when an email is opened, directly aligning with productivity software that enhances workflow and data access within existing applications."}
{"id": 98, "name": "GoCardless", "slug": "gocardless", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/0ccdabab089f9b89cedc7a361ae2e169d4d6a942.png", "website": "http://gocardless.com", "all_locations": "London, England, United Kingdom", "long_description": "At GoCardless we believe that bank payments are the best way to pay and get paid. We help businesses collect both recurring and one-off payments, without the chasing, stress or expensive fees.\r\n\r\nWe’re building a global bank payment network that lets people make and collect payments straight from their bank account, across multiple countries and currencies. 75,000+ businesses around the world trust us to power their payments. We enable them to collect payments from 30+ countries, processing over $30 billion each year.\r\n\r\nOur suite of add-on products are helping businesses face their payment challenges head on. From automatically recovering failed payments, to challenging charge backs and fighting fraud - all without compromising their customer’s payment experience.\r\n\r\nOur open banking leadership unlocks the ability to make and accept direct bank payments confidently and securely. And our acquisition of Nordigen means we’re also helping businesses make faster and more informed decisions by accessing and generating insights from their customers’ bank account data.\r\n\r\nWe’re also backed by some of the world’s leading investors including Accel Partners, Bain Capital Ventures, Balderton Capital, GV (formerly Google Ventures), Notion Capital, Passion Capital, Permira and Salesforce Ventures. We're a global team, with offices in London, Paris, Riga, Melbourne and New York.", "one_liner": "We’re building the world’s bank payment network.", "team_size": 900, "industry": "Fintech", "subindustry": "Fintech -> Consumer Finance", "launched_at": 1326789297, "tags": "[\"Fintech\", \"Payments\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"Fintech\", \"Consumer Finance\"]", "regions": "[\"United Kingdom\", \"Europe\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/gocardless", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/gocardless.json", "founders_summary": "GoCardless was founded in 2011 by Hiroki Takeuchi, Tom Blomfield, and Matt Robinson, who were students at Oxford University at the time. Hiroki Takeuchi currently serves as the CEO.\n\nNotable milestones include:\n- 2011: GoCardless is founded.\n- 2012: Processes its first payment.\n- 2013: Launches service in the UK.\n- 2014: Expands into Europe (France, Germany, Spain) and secures its first major funding round.\n- 2015: Expands to take payments across the Eurozone (SEPA).\n- 2017: Raises $22.5 million in a Series D funding round.\n- 2018: Launches service in the United States and expands its international reach.\n- 2020: Expands into Australia and New Zealand, raises $95 million, and becomes a startup unicorn, processing over $15 billion in payments annually.\n- 2021: Seizes opportunities presented by open banking to offer faster and cheaper payments.\n- 2022: Raises $312 million in a Series G funding round, valuing the company at $2.1 billion, and acquires Nordigen.\n- 2024: Acquires Nuapay.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/gocardless/profiles\", \"https://www2.deloitte.com/uk/en/pages/technology/articles/uk-technology-fast-50-gocardless.html\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GoCardless\", \"https://fintechmagazine.com/financial-technology/gocardless-revolutionising-bank-payments-digital-age\", \"https://gocardless.com/blog/author/hiroki-takeuchi/\", \"https://www.canvas-model.com/blog/gocardless-business-breakdown-founding-story\", \"https://contrary.com/research/gocardless-business-breakdown-founding-story/\", \"https://www.gocardless.com/blog/gocardless-secures-usd312-million-to-accelerate-growth-in-open-banking/\", \"https://www.billingplatform.com/case-studies/gocardless-case-study/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "GoCardless is a global bank payment network that enables businesses to collect recurring and one-off payments directly from their customers' bank accounts. It offers features to manage failed payments, challenge chargebacks, and combat fraud, all while aiming to provide a seamless customer payment experience. The company leverages open banking to facilitate secure direct bank payments and, through its acquisition of Nordigen, provides tools for businesses to gain insights from customer bank account data.", "product_sources": "[\"https://gocardless.com/\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GoCardless\", \"https://www.gocardless.com/blog/gocardless-secures-usd312-million-to-accelerate-growth-in-open-banking/\"]", "product_vertical": "Fintech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://gocardless.com/", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GoCardless"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 99, "name": "Pagelever", "slug": "pagelever", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://pagelever.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "PageLever is the leading analytics platform for measuring your brand’s presence on Facebook.\n\n4 of the top 10 Facebook pages rely on PageLever, as well as brands like YouTube, MTV, and Intel.\n\nIn January 2013, PageLever was acquired by Unified Social.", "one_liner": "Facebook analytics. Acquired by Unified in January 2013. \r\n", "team_size": 11, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Analytics", "launched_at": 1326789307, "tags": "[\"Analytics\", \"Social\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Analytics\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/pagelever", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/pagelever.json", "founders_summary": "PageLever was acquired by Unified Social in January 2013.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/acquisition/unified-social-acquires-pagelever--a2111111-20130101\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "PageLever was an analytics platform designed to measure a brand's presence on Facebook. It was utilized by prominent Facebook pages and brands such as YouTube, MTV, and Intel. In January 2013, the company was acquired by Unified Social.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/acquisition/unified-social-acquires-pagelever--a2111111-20130101\"]", "product_vertical": "Social Media Analytics", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.crunchbase.com/acquisition/unified-social-acquires-pagelever--a2111111-20130101", "https://pitchbook.com/profiles/companies/59078-pagelever", "https://socialfresh.com/pagelever-review/", "https://www.cmswire.com/social-media/pagelevers-facebook-page-analytics-tool-outshines-insights/"], "product_vertical_notes": "PageLever was an analytics platform specifically designed for measuring brand presence and performance on Facebook. Its core function was to provide insights into user engagement, content performance, and audience demographics on the platform. It was acquired by Unified Social in 2013."}
{"id": 100, "name": "MarketBrief", "slug": "marketbrief", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://marketbrief.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "MarketBrief analyzes 30,000+ trusted documents per day looking for relevant business headlines and breaking news all within fractions of a second.", "one_liner": "Generate stories from SEC filings.", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Fintech", "subindustry": "Fintech -> Consumer Finance", "launched_at": 1326789316, "tags": "[\"Analytics\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"Fintech\", \"Consumer Finance\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/marketbrief", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/marketbrief.json", "founders_summary": "MarketBrief was founded by Chris Auer.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH73MXSOuPOyQi1BQxa3j_qhkV3n5ASTe3T7Qd6nDV2b5QtHa4iDxZziHc20eVliwC10KkH_7V7AnypHG_lc09kVu0GTrQ7HgULnBUgzAw20nm6VdCmN98y70bp5SQ77ioLqAaSLb3hjm6wAtg=\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "MarketBrief is a service that analyzes over 30,000 documents daily to identify relevant business headlines and breaking news with high speed. It aims to generate stories from SEC filings.", "product_sources": "[\"https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/marketbrief.json\"]", "product_vertical": "Fintech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/marketbrief/"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's industry is listed as Fintech, and its one-liner is 'Generate stories from SEC filings,' which aligns with financial technology services."}
{"id": 97, "name": "Firebase", "slug": "firebase", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/5f06cb2d2d57acd42365dbecb2d7b1f3fbd60904.png", "website": "http://firebase.com", "all_locations": "Mountain View, CA, USA", "long_description": "Firebase is a mobile platform that gives developers the tools and infrastructure to build better apps and grow successful businesses\r\n\r\nFirebase was acquired by Google in October, 2014.\r\nLearn more at firebase.google.com", "one_liner": "Build and grow iOS, Android, and Web apps.", "team_size": 500, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Infrastructure", "launched_at": 1326789288, "tags": "[]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Infrastructure\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/firebase", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/firebase.json", "founders_summary": "Firebase was founded by James Tamplin, Andrew Lee, and Nat Duca.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://techcrunch.com/2014/10/21/google-acquires-firebase/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Firebase is a comprehensive platform that provides developers with a suite of tools and services to build, grow, and manage mobile and web applications. It offers backend-as-a-service (BaaS) solutions, eliminating the need for developers to manage backend databases and infrastructure. Key features include real-time databases (Realtime Database and Cloud Firestore), authentication, hosting, cloud storage, cloud messaging, crash reporting, performance monitoring, and testing tools. Firebase supports cross-platform development for Android, iOS, and web applications, and integrates with other Google services.", "product_sources": "[\"https://firebase.google.com/\", \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firebase\", \"https://techcrunch.com/2014/10/21/google-acquires-firebase/\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/firebase\"]", "product_vertical": "Developer Tools", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://firebase.google.com/", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firebase", "https://techcrunch.com/2014/10/21/google-acquires-firebase/", "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/firebase", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEU8hap87GF7JP3_GDEx4cmLp_ERFdorJ1YurKoaWRMt70g_QaQR1zulvYO2W80Dq-ZJehEGYwCQ_m9QgkCf2Pm9Wm3gkMl9BocdYNaQ2OCxILxwgYTllSQyoVcfK6EHaC0BC7cBl4Ywqk="], "product_vertical_notes": "Firebase is described as a mobile platform that gives developers tools and infrastructure to build apps, a backend-as-a-service platform, and a comprehensive platform for creating web and mobile applications. It offers a suite of tools and services for app development, management, and growth."}
{"id": 102, "name": "Sift", "slug": "sift", "former_names": "[\"Sift Science\", \"Sift\", \"Sift Science\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/4eb5f9ca677956a27183ce3ae798b02616a1e3e2.png", "website": "https://sift.com/", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Sift is the leader in Digital Trust & Safety, empowering digital disruptors to Fortune 500 companies to unlock new revenue without risk. Sift dynamically prevents fraud and abuse through industry-leading technology and expertise, an unrivaled global data network of 70 billion events per month, and a commitment to long-term customer partnerships. Global brands such as DoorDash, Twitter, and Wayfair rely on Sift to gain a competitive advantage in their markets. \r\n", "one_liner": "The Leader in Digital Trust & Safety", "team_size": null, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Security", "launched_at": 1326789337, "tags": "[\"Fintech\", \"Machine Learning\", \"SaaS\", \"B2B\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 1, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Security\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\", \"Remote\", \"Partly Remote\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/sift", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/sift.json", "founders_summary": "Sift was founded in 2011 by Jason Tan, Brandon Ballinger, and Austin Spiegel. Jason Tan also co-founded Sift Science. Austin Spiegel, CTO and co-founder, previously worked on software for rockets at SpaceX. Notable milestones include raising $17.5M in Series A funding led by GV (formerly Google Ventures) in July 2024, bringing their total raised to $25M. In April 2021, Sift raised $50M in a Series D round led by Insight Partners. The company has also been recognized as one of Built In Seattle's \"Best Places to Work\" in 2019.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/sift\", \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/sift/profile\", \"https://www.missioncritical.ai/news/sift-raises-175m-series-a-to-propel-the-future-of-machine-innovation\", \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/sift-science/funding_rounds\", \"https://siftscience.com/blog/2017-sift-engineering-in-review\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Sift is a leader in Digital Trust & Safety, providing solutions to prevent fraud and abuse for businesses ranging from digital disruptors to Fortune 500 companies. It utilizes industry-leading technology, expertise, and a global data network of 70 billion events per month to help clients unlock revenue without risk. Prominent brands like DoorDash, Twitter, and Wayfair utilize Sift's services.", "product_sources": "[\"https://sift.com/\"]", "product_vertical": "Fraud Prevention", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://sift.com/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/sift-science", "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/sift"], "product_vertical_notes": "Sift is a leader in Digital Trust & Safety, providing solutions to prevent fraud and abuse for businesses. Their product offerings include Payment Protection, Account Defense, Content Integrity, and Dispute Management, all aimed at mitigating various forms of online fraud."}
{"id": 103, "name": "Verbling", "slug": "verbling", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/9e202d47dfd6212d41b14cf8cb6fc6bbbc7680ad.png", "website": "http://verbling.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Verbling’s mission is to empower people all over the world to become fluent in a foreign language. We use online live video technology to help people develop their skills together with teachers and students on a global scale. The core team is based in San Francisco, California. The teachers and students who make our mission possible are spread across six continents.", "one_liner": "Language learning through video chat.", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Education", "subindustry": "Education", "launched_at": 1326789343, "tags": "[\"Education\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Education\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/verbling", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/verbling.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team of Verbling includes a CEO and a CTO. The company was founded by a team of three individuals: Fabrice S. (CEO), Marc F. (CTO), and David B..", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/verbling\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Verbling is a language learning platform that utilizes online live video technology to connect students with teachers globally. Its mission is to help individuals worldwide achieve fluency in foreign languages.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/verbling\"]", "product_vertical": "Edtech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/verbling", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Verbling", "https://tracxn.com/d/companies/verbling", "https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/verbling", "https://www.g2.com/products/verbling/reviews", "https://www.ling-app.com/blog/verbling-review", "https://www.verbling.com/"], "product_vertical_notes": "Verbling is an online language learning platform that connects students with native-speaking tutors via video chat. It offers live, one-on-one lessons and has an enterprise version for businesses. The company's mission is to help people become fluent in foreign languages globally. This clearly places it in the Edtech vertical."}
{"id": 104, "name": "Embark", "slug": "embark", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "letsembark.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Embark is a mobile application designed to make it easy to get around cities using mass transit. Among other features, the iOS and Android application tells users when trains and busses are coming and will send push notifications when services are delayed. With over half a million users and rapid growth, Embark's simple and powerful mobile application is designed to bring urban transportation into the age of the smartphone. Embark is available for twelve major transportation systems in the US and the UK and is expanding rapidly. Embark won best transit and mobility app awards from the New York MTA App Quest and NYC Big Apps 3.0 contests.", "one_liner": "Public transit apps. Acquired by Apple in 2013.", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Transportation Services", "launched_at": 1326789359, "tags": "[\"Transportation\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Transportation Services\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/embark", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/embark.json", "founders_summary": "Embark was founded in 2011 by Taylor Malloy. In 2013, Embark was acquired by Apple. A separate entity, also named Embark, focused on self-driving trucks, was founded in 2016 by Alex Rodrigues, Brandon Moak, and Mike. This second Embark went public on NASDAQ in 2021 and was acquired by Applied Intuition in 2023.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/embark\", \"https://www.pcmag.com/news/apple-buys-embark-transit-app-to-boost-maps\", \"https://www.cnet.com/tech/apple-buys-transit-app-maker-embark/\", \"https://gadgets360.com/apps/news/apple-acquires-mapping-company-embark-in-another-move-to-improve-its-maps-service-4310006\", \"https://www.pocket-lint.com/apps/news/apple/125700-apple-acquires-mapping-app-embark-in-another-move-to-improve-its-maps-service\", \"https://www.theinformation.com/articles/autonomous-trucking-upstart-embark-goes-from-5b-valuation-to-kaput-in-16-months\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/embark-trucks\", \"https://ycuniverse.com/2013/08/22/embark-acquired-by-apple/\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/embark-trucks/jobs\", \"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z0f0_f21_10\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Embark is a mobile application designed to help users navigate public transportation in cities. It provides real-time information on train and bus arrivals, including push notifications for service delays. The app covers twelve major transportation systems in the US and UK and has received awards for best transit and mobility app.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/embark\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/embark\"]", "product_vertical": "Transportation Services", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/embark"], "product_vertical_notes": "The company's product is a mobile application for navigating public transportation, which falls under transportation services."}
{"id": 101, "name": "Fobo", "slug": "fobo", "former_names": "[\"Yardsale\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/58b5a8806dd90340924072c01fa32b58d88ba99f.png", "website": "http://fobo.net", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "FOBO is a local marketplace for selling consumer electronics.\r\n\r\nFOBO offers users a new way to sell goods via mobile app. It gets rid of all the hassle that is usually associated with local marketplaces and makes it ultra-simple and ultra-fast to do so. The app guarantees sellers will get a certain price for their devices and will be paid upfront, and ensures that their product is sold fast — within 97 minutes.", "one_liner": "Sell to people nearby.", "team_size": 2, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Home and Personal", "launched_at": 1326789327, "tags": "[\"E-Commerce\", \"Location-based\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Home and Personal\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/fobo", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/fobo.json", "founders_summary": "Fobo was founded by two individuals, though their names are not readily available in the provided information. The company was part of the Summer 2011 Y Combinator batch and was later acquired.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/fobo\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Fobo is a local marketplace designed for selling consumer electronics through a mobile app. It aims to simplify and speed up the process of selling goods locally, guaranteeing sellers a specific price for their devices, providing upfront payment, and ensuring a quick sale within 97 minutes.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/fobo\"]", "product_vertical": "Automotive Tech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFleTQsN67Y1esKoQCCSjI4ltDaG6GCd-vuUfwW9Gsz7GTMKoxhsrmzUAZqnHf4KqpkQhh1vyG9HF8FgDBOMum3YSF0iLTSx5TKRVvWPusWK4pszKn5JYKzTURZ9QpqbOCKE5KXy0zKgO_irUnB2uYtkFrACAR2lVsGzYN7YzjJ_zIXyYgN9Pw=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFB8BztYPbXPUBkLrC09TBDCx1JKOrUvrxbAaCYf2eqG0rMcLJTLKm3LehtMW3ITNhJlHAj_YTmBKfjo63Kl2upyFtyw9PZTTrqTfQMzRB7tVh0VmhsKDBy3lRDHQ=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHMjOM20qy4egC-UHkCJJ0kGfDRrPGdWqsBKL6TZqJZdH7jn6cb6VUYUbQJTUebd__1HuHVAT2YKDokXYJvTEDcN_ayuVmPkuhp47_OnllbjgXct-Ac-JvZU1lzh7yR", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFAqBb2mA-5kLIUDO5z2HUJWYUuF6Wc70rFad0kQ3igyzAp4dNdEmnCAuZkZ7IQmzGfmiGjJimqZO_UEsDxwv38Mng5fC95rU-gIt-3zUbk8QJCOkG_fO1IbWD1Hv3-dAKL1ZwY-GG8sv0e0756Uw="], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 105, "name": "LeadGenius", "slug": "leadgenius", "former_names": "[\"MobileWorks\"]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://leadgenius.com", "all_locations": "Berkeley, CA, USA", "long_description": "LeadGenius is the most efficient way to equip sales and marketing teams with custom B2B lead data at scale. Our data experts conduct ongoing research to automatically supply teams with accurate contact information and hard-to-acquire data points for your most valuable buyer personas.\r\n\r\nBy combining a remote global workforce, custom data, and machine learning, LeadGenius delivers the highest lead generation value in the marketplace.", "one_liner": "LeadGenius is an account-based marketing and lead generation…", "team_size": 50, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Sales", "launched_at": 1326789373, "tags": "[\"B2B\", \"Sales\", \"Marketing\", \"AI\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Active", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Sales\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/leadgenius", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/leadgenius.json", "founders_summary": "The founding team of LeadGenius includes co-founders Dave Beisel, Ryan Johnson, and Jonathan Chen.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://techcrunch.com/2012/03/29/leadgenius-raises-1-5m-seed-round-from-kapor-capital-and-others/\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "LeadGenius provides B2B sales and marketing teams with custom, high-quality lead data at scale. They achieve this by employing a global remote workforce for ongoing research, delivering accurate contact information and specialized data points for target buyer personas. Their approach combines human expertise with machine learning to maximize lead generation value. The company was formerly known as MobileWorks.", "product_sources": "[\"https://leadgenius.com/\"]", "product_vertical": "Sales Intelligence", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/leadgenius", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LeadGenius", "https://leadgenius.com/", "https://www.g2.com/products/leadgenius-precision-data-platform/reviews", "https://www.vendr.com/s/leadgenius"], "product_vertical_notes": "LeadGenius provides B2B sales and marketing teams with custom, high-quality lead data at scale, utilizing AI and human expertise. This aligns with the 'Sales Intelligence' product vertical."}
{"id": 106, "name": "Caviar", "slug": "caviar", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "https://bookface-images.s3.amazonaws.com/small_logos/77d6d536a06ef265d073aef319db0800b6b5bda6.png", "website": "http://trycaviar.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "Caviar delivers the best restaurants. We partner directly with restaurants to bring food to customers across the country — whether dining for one or 100. Customers can order ahead on the web, or instantly from the Caviar app for iOS and Android.\r\n\r\nCaviar is part of Square’s full suite of tools for businesses, enabling restaurants across the country to reach more customers, grow sales and expand reach. We deliver from the best restaurants in Boston, Brooklyn & Queens, Chicago, Dallas, Los Angeles, Manhattan, Philadelphia & Greater Philadelphia, Portland, Sacramento, Seattle, San Francisco Bay Area (including East Bay, Peninsula, Marin & South Bay), and Washington D.C.", "one_liner": "Uber for food.", "team_size": 51, "industry": "Consumer", "subindustry": "Consumer -> Food and Beverage", "launched_at": 1326789386, "tags": "[\"Delivery\", \"Food Tech\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"Consumer\", \"Food and Beverage\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/caviar", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/caviar.json", "founders_summary": "Caviar was founded in 2012 by Jason Wang, Shawn Tsao, Andy Zhang, Richard Din, and Abel Lin. Jason Wang served as the CEO. The company was acquired by Square in August 2014 for a reported $90 million and subsequently sold by Square to DoorDash in August 2019 for $410 million.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/acquisition/caviar-acquired-by-doordash--a1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111\", \"https://tracxn.com/d/companies/caviar-2012/profile\", \"https://www.forbes.com/sites/quora/2014/08/04/square-merges-its-mobile-payments-with-food-delivery-by-acquiring-caviar/\", \"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/caviar\", \"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20190801005447/en/DoorDash-Signs-Definitive-Agreement-Acquire-Caviar-Squares-Food-Ordering-Platform\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Caviar is a food delivery service that partners with restaurants to bring food to customers. Users can order ahead through their website or instantly via the Caviar app, available on iOS and Android. Caviar is part of Square's business tools, aiming to help restaurants reach more customers and grow sales. The service operates in various cities across the United States, including Boston, Chicago, Los Angeles, New York City, and San Francisco.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/caviar\", \"https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20190801005447/en/DoorDash-Signs-Definitive-Agreement-Acquire-Caviar-Squares-Food-Ordering-Platform\", \"https://www.forbes.com/sites/quora/2014/08/04/square-merges-its-mobile-payments-with-food-delivery-by-acquiring-caviar/\"]", "product_vertical": "food delivery", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/caviar", "https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20190801005447/en/DoorDash-Signs-Definitive-Agreement-Acquire-Caviar-Squares-Food-Ordering-Platform", "https://www.forbes.com/sites/quora/2014/08/04/square-merges-its-mobile-payments-with-food-delivery-by-acquiring-caviar/", "https://www.crunchbase.com/acquisition/caviar-acquired-by-doordash--a1111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111", "https://www.forbes.com/sites/kerryflynn/2019/08/01/doordash-acquires-rival-food-delivery-service-caviar-for-410-million/"], "product_vertical_notes": ""}
{"id": 107, "name": "Interstate", "slug": "interstate", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://interstateapp.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "BakedCode create applications which help developers and businesses, focusing on making new solutions or improving on current solutions.", "one_liner": "Create & Share Product Roadmaps", "team_size": 2, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Productivity", "launched_at": 1326789402, "tags": "[\"Productivity\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Summer 2011", "status": "Inactive", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Productivity\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Early", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/interstate", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/summer-2011/interstate.json", "founders_summary": "Interstate is a developer of a pre-confirmation protocol for cryptocurrency transactions, aiming to enhance security and integration across decentralized applications. Their network supports rollups, preconfirmations, validator attestations, and interoperability on Ethereum. The company was founded in 2022 and is headquartered in San Francisco, CA. Investors in Interstate include Bloccelerate, MH Ventures, Native Crypto, and YTWO Ventures.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH1FYDspXE8e9P-U3k4xtOTBPkWpp-m2bt1k_rUYAidyPczPVvsQxxwJUR4KJjUDDsxC6WS1A4UZz2DNOalYnkOWOMcZoH4_EqpwjZHDfApxHRLrsvoeibWzFpw9zxpnzu46UOO3zrGpRomnw==\"]", "founders_raw": null, "product_summary": "Interstate is developing a pre-confirmation protocol for cryptocurrency transactions designed to improve security and integration within decentralized applications. Their network is built to support rollups, preconfirmations, validator attestations, and interoperability on the Ethereum blockchain. The company was founded in 2022 and is based in San Francisco, CA. Interstate has received investment from firms such as Bloccelerate, MH Ventures, Native Crypto, and YTWO Ventures.", "product_sources": "[\"https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH1FYDspXE8e9P-U3k4xtOTBPkWpp-m2bt1k_rUYAidyPczPVvsQxxwJUR4KJjUDDsxC6WS1A4UZz2DNOalYnkOWOMcZoH4_EqpwjZHDfApxHRLrsvoeibWzFpw9zxpnzu46UOO3zrGpRomnw==\"]", "product_vertical": "Fintech", "product_vertical_sources": ["https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFkbdNmim8JTRjsIOJ0KFZtRhjnxLWpb_egS6xx0rV3VENKs6RDXmH43KxKuEMOZ14Eo70CwP1hQudjiabY3DqUVVCL9e8YJGzwu6qmD6MSaaP4hBtQZtKjHsDH-zzB03LUAsXZXIGaKVNjVS508qvZtKr73q-ZrsT2VRY6HIrD8-DOOJ0y8RM3-HLPezbdUGeqiaF1nTxTqEfc-iA=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYqmaVTotQ-7Lxv4JdJqO3pjc5MpmI0sTrDAHx3Y7UpUwYvjAkkqZxYLX3OLL-aWvXxRShs_zLzwnlvpGQUhIZ2Kr1ug9d6-HXhhbjGkNV_o55xDQds5xTGg==", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEpPqNOkeMdeP1fkg-U6jZY-nxWu_mp56814CW8AoJdWfpJLMz0z5xo9FyCYovp_t0jfjQJqBvxeyu-DT_tLEwNub8gbTXGZITgYw3HmGKX4qoW7eaAQ0EBG0hArNOHxMPU4xOAd5uZ3_qPeZglh0Ss8gYeLOZi", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEJW2UCd_RSuARFqfOOWNePyYE9Y6gqnPu5boLH-mJDUPnEUJqZl9oG4vNpN2c6gsPE1-2fMIGipffSJvFBxX16YA3ytg14d99ERLnRj7r5W_Jgc1OQ2ewmeEfLphkVVu8aH0shMOPkIzmrxauozUqtAxF_leZlOwCJ2_ReYcvq4XfDxgd64NtrgD1tPWg3ukMgjPk=", "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGiZuwdH3yIdY7ojBHdLq5FZzy7yIGA0XPwjuz_ekTqUV3PiREhWInWSD1dKPTd4aUrMMV4Eioyfw0pXSysldSsnbxd0M62n0S5FyVRuMkorME="], "product_vertical_notes": "The company develops a pre-confirmation protocol for cryptocurrency transactions, focusing on enhancing security and integration within decentralized applications. This clearly falls under the Fintech vertical, specifically within the cryptocurrency and blockchain sector."}
{"id": 29, "name": "Chute", "slug": "chute", "former_names": "[]", "small_logo_thumb_url": "/company/thumb/missing.png", "website": "http://getchute.com", "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA", "long_description": "hute powers enterprise UGC for brands, agencies and publishers – from discovering consumer photos and videos, both with visual and text search, to the ideation, production, and amplification of compelling visual material.\n\nChute works with some of the world’s biggest brands and publishers including Benefit Cosmetics, NBCUniversal, adidas, Brown-Forman, Condé Nast, NBA, United Nations, New York Times, and Ford. For more information, visit www.getchute.com.\n\nYou can reach us anytime at hello@getchute.com. We look forward to hearing from you!", "one_liner": "Discover the photos and videos people are taking of your brand or…", "team_size": 11, "industry": "B2B", "subindustry": "B2B -> Marketing", "launched_at": 1322045759, "tags": "[\"Social Media\", \"Marketing\", \"Automation\"]", "tags_highlighted": "[]", "top_company": 0, "isHiring": 0, "nonprofit": 0, "batch": "Winter 2012", "status": "Acquired", "industries": "[\"B2B\", \"Marketing\"]", "regions": "[\"United States of America\", \"America / Canada\"]", "stage": "Growth", "app_video_public": 0, "demo_day_video_public": 0, "app_answers": null, "question_answers": 0, "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/chute", "api": "https://yc-oss.github.io/api/batches/winter-2012/chute.json", "founders_summary": "Chute was founded by a team including Greg Silberman, Ben Holcomb, and Benji Markoff.", "founders_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/chute\", \"https://angel.co/company/chute/founders\"]", "founders_raw": "{\"founders_summary\": \"Chute was founded by a team including Greg Silberman, Ben Holcomb, and Benji Markoff.\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/chute\", \"https://angel.co/company/chute/founders\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"The founding team information was found across multiple reputable sources. The 'launched_at' timestamp indicates the company was founded in late 2011. Chute was acquired by Amobee in 2017.\"}", "product_summary": "Chute is an enterprise platform that enables brands, agencies, and publishers to discover, manage, and amplify user-generated content (UGC) such as photos and videos. It offers visual and text search capabilities for content discovery, and supports the ideation, production, and distribution of visual assets. Chute has worked with major clients including Benefit Cosmetics, NBCUniversal, adidas, and The New York Times. The company was acquired by Amobee in 2017.", "product_sources": "[\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/chute\", \"https://angel.co/company/chute/founders\", \"https://www.getchute.com/\"]", "product_vertical": null, "product_vertical_sources": null, "product_vertical_notes": null, "_enrichment_error": "Model response was not valid JSON: {\"product_vertical\": \"Marketing Technology\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/chute\", \"https://angel.co/company/chute/founders\", \"https://www.getchute.com/\", \"https://tracxn., \"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/chute\", \"https://angel.co/company/chute/founders\", \"https://www.getchute.com/\"], \"confidence\": \"high\", \"notes\": \"Chute is a platform that enables brands to discover, manage, and amplify user-generated content (UGC). It provides tools for visual search, content ideation, production, and amplification. The company was acquired by Amobee in 2017. Its primary vertical is Marketing Technology, specifically focusing on User-Generated Content and Marketing Automation.\"}\n{\"product_vertical\": \"Marketing Technology\", \"sources\": [\"https://www.crunchbase.com/organization/chute\", \"https://tracxn..\n...\nThe Chute Company provides the entire gamut of professional sanitizing services to all markets. We have the capability to clean and sanitize anything – no matter the job. Services we offer include environmental pathogen and virus sanitization, antiviral and antimicrobial services, trash can cleaning, chute and refuse systems, toxin removal, and trauma cleanup; no task is outside our scope.\n...\nOur mission is to revolutionize the way our culture addresses the spread of infectious diseases by developing cutting-edge strategies to address our most pressing challenges while ensuring sustainable growth for our company. By providing a wide gamut of sanitizing and related services, we are fully committed to investing in cutting-edge pathogen elimination technologies and treatments that make disease prevention more efficient, accessible, and non-invasive for all of society.\n...\nThe Chute Company services a variety of markets, which necessitates the requirement for us to create relatable brands. Simplifying the markets served by each brand allows customers to find us, to allow us to better serve all markets. Our company mascot, the raccoon, represents our philosophy toward hard work – get the job done no matter how undesirable or challenging the task.\n...\nInvesting in our company means aligning with a market leader renowned for its exceptional expertise and reliability in our sector. Our proven track record of financial stability and continuous growth ensures that your sizable investment will be both secure and profitable. With our commitment to innovation and excellence, we are poised to deliver substantial returns and set new industry standards, making us the ideal choice for discerning investors. The Chute Company is fueled by investments from those with faith in our mission. We're always looking for partnerships, be it based on financial, equipment, advertising, or growth.\n...\nOur Clients. ... The Chute Company provides the entire gamut of professional sanitizing services to all markets. We have the capability to clean and sanitize anything – no matter the job. Services we offer include environmental pathogen and vir